{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine","id":465635,"title":"Replacing the \"God Machine\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-01T21:46:15-07:00","id":465635,"title":"Replacing the \"God Machine\"","content":"I really love the NWOD setting and the streamlined systems. But then Demon the Descent moved away from true demons and introduced the &quot;God Machine&quot;. I absolutely hate this concept. I was wondering if anyone knew of a way to completely remove Demon the Descent and replace it with cWOD Demon the Fallen but still use the NWOD systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5542-revanauditore92","name":"revanauditore92","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T22:29:08-07:00","id":465676,"title":"","content":"You could just not play Demon the Descent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T22:34:12-07:00","id":465680,"title":"","content":"There's plenty of material in 1e that can be interpreted as belonging to that particular gameline. The God Machine was something that started out as fluff, and then interest in it spiraled into the GM getting its own chronicle. There are plenty of hooks to build on that you don't need D:tD \u2014 such is the sandbox nature of WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T22:39:23-07:00","id":465682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>revanauditore92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine#post465635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering if anyone knew of a way to completely remove Demon the Descent and replace it with cWOD Demon the Fallen but still use the NWOD systems.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Demon Translation Guide is being worked on which will bring Fallen into nWoD. It will be a while though. I believe there's a fan made update of Fallen to nWoD floating around somewhere but I haven't seen it in a while. Hope that helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1279-badger-king","user":"Badger King","date":".  Original post made me sound like a jerk 04-02-2015, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1279-badger-king","name":"Badger King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1279_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T23:08:34-07:00","id":465706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>revanauditore92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine#post465635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then Demon the Descent moved away from true demons and introduced the &quot;God Machine&quot;. I absolutely hate this concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your complaint is vague, your terminology is poorly defined, and your opinion is utterly irrelevant to the reasonable thing you are asking after, all of which is business as usual for this type of discussion, which has been had multiple times with an overabundance of vitriol.<br /> <br /> Literally the only thing you had to do was ask if there was a Translation Guide in the works for Demon: the Fallen, as there has been one for Vampire: the Masquerade, Werewolf: the Apocalypse, and Mage: the Ascension; as has been highlighted above, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide\">there is indeed a DtF/DtD Translation Guide being written</a>, and as highlighted above, there is no force employed by Onyx Path Publishing that can cause you to play Demon: the Descent against your will.*<br /> <br /> * I would put a jocularly menacing &quot;<i>Yet.</i>&quot; here, but experience suggests this is an unwise line of frivolity to pursue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T23:23:42-07:00","id":465714,"title":"","content":"To give a slightly less cheeky response than my first post, could you be more specific about what you mean by &quot;true demons&quot;? Aside from the technological aesthetic (which is actually not that crucial to D:tD), they are very good examples of the fallen angel concept. They used to be angels, they failed to carry out God's plan, fell from grace, and now hide among humanity from their vengeful creator. They make deals for people's souls like you would expect a demon to do. True, they're more former angels in the process of falling than full-on post-fall devils, and the setting's dogma is a little on the Gnostic side, but they are very much true demons in my book. If the machine aspect is all that bothers you, it's really easy to just ignore that part, and doesn't damage the play or mechanics at all. If you have a different problem with their demon-ness, you'll need to be more specific about what that problem is. There is a translation guide in the works to convert D:tF to D:tD and vice-versa, but it's going to take a while and in the mean time your options pretty much boil down to re-fluffing D:tD to fit within your view of what &quot;true demons&quot; are, or not playing D:tD. And there's nothing wrong with the latter option if you genuinely hate D:tD. The world of darkness got on fine without it for almost 10 years before D:tD was written, there's no reason you can't just continue playing without involving demons in your games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T23:47:30-07:00","id":465733,"title":"","content":"I shouldn't, but I must say something. So, after picking through the myraid of my usual responses, I just want to ask:<br /> <br /> Is &quot;God&quot; so much better a concept than a &quot;God-Machine&quot;?<br /> <br /> I'll stop there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T00:10:32-07:00","id":465754,"title":"","content":"Replace god-machine with Azothoth, and boom you have a game of eldritch abominations pretending to be humans with magical powers that are magic from technology hiding from a lovecraftian deity.<br /> <br /> No, wait, demon the descent is already a game about eldritch abominations pretending to be humans with magical powers that are magic from technology while hiding from a lovecraftian deity. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, to the OP, you may want to buy inferno, which covers the demons from various religions as spirits of sin, and has rules for demonic pacts and those possessed by such demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 04-02-2015, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T00:47:30-07:00","id":465763,"title":"","content":"Speaking as a huge Descent fan, and someone who will argue that it has plenty of influence from more traditional stories of demons and angels? Yeah, it honestly isn't that easy to run without the God Machine.<br /> <br /> It's not at all hard to run without <i>the technological aesthetic.</i> Rename the demonic form abilities (I took a stab <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/205376-homebrew-demon-translation-lexicon?p=209384#post209384\">here</a>), replace descriptions of draining aetheric waste-heat from infrastructure with lines about hunting down and devouring the divine spark from modern sacred sites and disguised hallows, talk about Embeds tapping into the secret laws of Creation rather than hacking into the logistical substrata of the universe, call cryptids nephilim, you've got a solid spy game about more classical fallen angels in the modern world.<br /> <br /> But the &quot;machine&quot; part of the God Machine that's hard to remove isn't the part where it has gears and furnaces and its angels have syringes for fingers. It's the part where God isn't numinous, where God is a part of the world and his will is manifest through physical plans that can be interrupted. That's good for Descent's poststructuralist social critique, and it's great for gameplay where you have attainable goals and clear results of your achievements, but it's not a traditional representation.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, if you want to run something more like Fallen, you have an out. Fallen is sometimes implied to take place in a world where the Creator and His angelic host have departed from the world in the wake of a primeval fall that broke the world. Just run with half of that. Angels are still around, but in the absence of the Creator, they're weak, they've become the ephemeral angels of Descent with statblocks whom you can defeat, and who depend on what energies of creation they can produce from mortal loyalties to manifest and sustain themselves (a.k.a. non-technological Infrastructure \u2014 angelic cults, holy laborers and blessed hidden sanctuaries). Rather than the eye of the God Machine, you adopt human Cover to evade the remnants of the angelic host, while you do whatever fallen angel things your character does \u2014 get your filthy hands on temporal influence or occult power, seek revenge on the angels, repent and do what good you can in the spaces between, try to figure out what's going on and, perhaps, get closer to the universal plan than the scattered and confused angels are now. Hey, look at that, those are basically the four Agendas!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T00:50:54-07:00","id":465770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=465733#post465733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I shouldn't, but I must say something. So, after picking through the myraid of my usual responses, I just want to ask:<br /> <br /> Is &quot;God&quot; so much better a concept than a &quot;God-Machine&quot;?<br /> <br /> I'll stop there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This. God-Machine is so much better than &quot;God&quot; :P <br /> <br /> And as others have stated, refluffing everything is pretty easy, to fit other religions, an omnipowerful being, demons... as long as you don't mind their powers being focused on hiding/espionage and a little bit more on technology (but those can be dropped)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T02:48:31-07:00","id":465846,"title":"","content":"I love Demon, but it is very easy to run New WoD without it. The easiest way to remove it is just not use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T03:06:59-07:00","id":465859,"title":"","content":"First things first, nothing is concrete in the nWoD. If you don't like the God-Machine, you just say it doesn't exist, and it doesn't; you aren't violating canon or anything, like with oWoD. D:tD is a fantastic game and really deserves a second look. Once you drop your expectations of classic Abrahamic demons, you'll find a stellar urban fantasy-horror espionage game.<br /> <br /> If you want more old-school demons, then <i>Inferno</i> has you covered, complete with the Possessed; folks ridden by critters of the Seven Sins. Hunter: the Vigil adds a playable group called the Lucifuge, who are mortals with the blood of Hell running through their veins. And then there's the Translation Guide for Demon on the horizon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T04:39:47-07:00","id":465919,"title":"","content":"What exactly do you not like? If it's just the bio-tech aesthetic then it's easy enough to trade that out for Christian imagery. I say Christian because Jewish angels can be pretty bizarre, and hellfire and brimstone and angels with dove wings is basically a Christian thing.<br /> <br /> Without detailing any other opinion I might have, I will say that, while <b>Demon: the Descent</b> does everything right while exploring new territory as it retains the 'fallen angel' concept, if ever I ran it I would probably wait for the <b>Translation Guide</b>, too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T16:23:08-07:00","id":466631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>revanauditore92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine#post465635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really love the NWOD setting and the streamlined systems. But then Demon the Descent moved away from true demons and introduced the &quot;God Machine&quot;. I absolutely hate this concept. I was wondering if anyone knew of a way to completely remove Demon the Descent and replace it with cWOD Demon the Fallen but still use the NWOD systems.</div> </div> </div> </div><ul><li>Use Inferno adapted to the revised rules</li> <li>Use the strix from Blood and Smoke</li> <li>Use the Myriad of types of Demons from Mage</li> <li>You could adapt the Angels/demons from Promethean</li> </ul>God Machine setting is optional. Take whatever you want file off the serial numbers and use it for your own purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T20:37:36-07:00","id":466939,"title":"","content":"Mortal Remains ( a hunter book ) sort of reframes the descent demons as not necessarily technological. (&quot;Sort of&quot; should be very loosely understood.) <br /> The demons that hunters talk to don't talk about the God-machine so much as the &quot;Demiurge&quot;, the gnostic God of this world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T22:17:12-07:00","id":467004,"title":"","content":"Descent feels too much like the Matrix to me. I prefer my angels and demons to be rooted in the spirtual and mystical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5542-revanauditore92","name":"revanauditore92","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T22:18:26-07:00","id":467006,"title":"","content":"For real, you can very easily completely ignore all of the technological stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T23:46:31-07:00","id":467071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>revanauditore92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=467004#post467004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Descent feels too much like the Matrix to me. I prefer my angels and demons to be rooted in the spirtual and mystical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't really think of something more spiritual than Gnosticism, which Demon and The Matrix rely heavily upon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T00:14:00-07:00","id":467080,"title":"","content":"The Gnostic bits in Demon are frankly some of the most fascinating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T00:42:51-07:00","id":467091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>revanauditore92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=467004#post467004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Descent feels too much like the Matrix to me. I prefer my angels and demons to be rooted in the spirtual and mystical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there are other demons to use. Including, Astral, Supernal, Abyssal, and Infernal. So if you want mystical demons, they are there.<br /> If you want mystical angels, there are the Quashmalim and the angels of the Aether. Pretty mystical both of them.<br /> <br /> And it's not like anything is an integral part of the setting. Any- and everything is easy to just remove.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T04:16:09-07:00","id":467199,"title":"","content":"I gotta say, the amount of condescending hostility towards the OP is extremely off-putting. No he's not making a comment/request that hasn't been made many times before by many other people, but perhaps instead of ridiculing him for that we can recognize that for a notable number of old NWoD fans and customers the Techgnostic themes of the Godmachine are not an appealing undercurrent?<br /> <br /> You can say all you want that &quot;just run it without those themes&quot;, but the mere fact that so many posters come here with that very complaint gives word to the lie that they are so easily ignored or excised.<br /> <br /> Either way, can we be a little more kind to new posters? Just because we've seen the same things many times before should not put a burden on all new posters to do research into this community's meta-discussion of certain topics... and if it is so egregious as to warrant hostility then can we get sticky posts for such ongoing discussions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","user":"Anachronistic Jam","date":". 04-03-2015, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T04:57:36-07:00","id":467224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>revanauditore92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=467004#post467004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Descent feels too much like the Matrix to me. I prefer my angels and demons to be rooted in the spirtual and mystical.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it can be done.<br /> <br /> First- the God Machine. Let's just drop the Machine part. Instead, treat as as what it is- a distant, cold, logical divinity who manipulates thousands of people to proceed with its projects. Infrastructures don't has to be mechanical- they are forms of sacred geometry, like Ley Lines or any other similar ideas. Instead of saying Gears, you can see it as God's Hands, Ears and Eyes- for God see all, hears all and acts everywhere. The trick is that God is not as strong as the stories claim- maybe he never was omnipotent, just a single powerful divinity who rose higher then the rest. Maybe He was more powerful in the past, but has lost some of His power through a &quot;failed project&quot; of some kind. What ever the truth is, God has became much more dependent on his Angels and cultists.<br /> <br /> As for Angels, it is easy to just through away the machine-like visage and replace it with plane weird aesthetics. Many eyes, beast heads, alien bodies, perfect and terrible beauty. Each is devoted to a single mission- there is not need to change it. Angel in Hebrew (or Malakh) means &quot;messenger&quot;, after all. They are inhumane beings who manifest in the world, searching to fulfill God's will. However, taking a human form also means being subject to human emotions- and while usually walking on God's path would protect them, defying their mission would make them stray too much from the Great Plan and fall, turning their false lives into truth- at least, a form of truth. Angels can sin in human body- and that sin turns them into Demons.<br /> <br /> Once they are Unchained, they lose touch with God- and he starts searching after them. Demons shouldn't exist, and so they mess up with His Great Design. As long as they disguise themselves as humans, the Angels can't find their Divine Aura. They no longer have Rank, instead gaining power from their own, personal Divinity (instead of Primum). The also no longer consume Essence, finding energy in the Shell that are left behind after God's projects, or Qlipoth (instead of Aether). Being creatures of divine power, they can manipulate the souls of humans and rip the divine structure of reality for their own benefit- in the forms of Pacts. That process allows them taking parts of the human's place in reality in order to create lives of their own, and they can even possess the whole human and through his soul to Hell. Demon, however, can't enter there- God needs all the angels He has, and so he captures them and break their essence in order to make a fresh start. Hell is the only place He can't reach- and so they seek after a way to get in. Until then, a human body would be enough. Sometimes, they can even meld their essence into God's creation in order to take one of his forms as Cover- but it is a risky process which allows Him to notice you.<br /> <br /> Finally, about their powers- Embeds could be called &quot;Jewellery&quot;, or even Hoshen. (the biblical stone decorated breastplate of the high priest). Exploits are now Invocations. Demonic Form abilities are called Transformations for Modifications, Symbols for Technologies, Movement for Propulsions and Visages for Processes. Finally, Ciphers would be Keys.<br /> <br /> As for antagonists- Angels are as described. Exiles are angels who still walk on God's Path, but didn't returned to him when the mission was over- or simply screwed up too much. Cryptids could be called as Haiot HaKodesh (&quot;the holy beasts&quot;). Stigmatics are people touched by God- you could either keep their name or call them Prophets, both could work. They can see his divine projects everywhere, so they can get a bit mad.<br /> <br /> That's it, I think. Hope it helped with something :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T06:19:04-07:00","id":467273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=465919#post465919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly do you not like? If it's just the bio-tech aesthetic then it's easy enough to trade that out for Christian imagery. I say Christian because Jewish angels can be pretty bizarre, and hellfire and brimstone and angels with dove wings is basically a Christian thing.<br /> <br /> Without detailing any other opinion I might have, I will say that, while <b>Demon: the Descent</b> does everything right while exploring new territory as it retains the 'fallen angel' concept, if ever I ran it I would probably wait for the <b>Translation Guide</b>, too</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno where you get that Jewish imagery isn't perfect. I think a literal flaming eye-covered entity composed of two nested wheels (See: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ophanim\" target=\"_blank\">ophanim</a>) sort of fits with the sort of oddity in form that's represented by the current God Machine demons. The lack of 'dove wings' in Jewish lore doesn't necessarily preclude our mythology's fitting in with what's shown here. Also, concepts such as nephilim are definitely from our lore first, which puts Heirs of Hell back in play. And the lack of a Hell (beyond the vague concept of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sheol\" target=\"_blank\">Sheol</a>, which is about being cut off from God's light and love...oh, wait) is also in line with Demon as written; if you need a Hell, you have to build it for yourself, or find it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T06:30:52-07:00","id":467299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>revanauditore92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=467004#post467004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Descent feels too much like the Matrix to me. I prefer my angels and demons to be rooted in the spirtual and mystical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not trying to sound like a smart-ass, but I think its funny that you contrasted mysticism and spirituality with <i>The Matrix,</i> of all things.<br /> <br /> Also, going to Nth everyone's suggestions here. You can pretty much file off the aesthetic bits you don't like without much trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T08:23:01-07:00","id":467412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>revanauditore92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=467004#post467004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Descent feels too much like the Matrix to me. I prefer my angels and demons to be rooted in the spirtual and mystical.</div> </div> </div> </div> The irony is that the God Machine is rooted very strongly in the spiritual and mystical. If anything, it draws from far more mystical and spiritual traditions than Demon the Fallen.<br /> <br /> Like others have said, its simplicity within itself to just ignore the machine bits. There's nothing in the game that depends on God being a literal machine. Infrastructure, occult matrix? These are just fancy words for ritual components and the actual ritual itself. God needs the right person (divine-chosen bloodlines) in the right place (geomancy) at the right time (when the stars align) to work its miracles. You can play a red skinned devil with horns, goat legs, a tail, and hellfire powers, or a manipulative, hedonistic, addictive succubus, or an imp, or even a lion headed wheel with spinning legs of fire. The spy thing is just the continuing war between the forces of Heaven and Hell in a way that's hidden from human eyes. <br /> <br /> <br /> Playing the game without the machine bits is insanely easy. Everything you could want for making a classical-Christian-themed demon is there, just under different names. Even demon summoning is possible. Now, if you don't like the idea of a covert war between Angels and Demons, that's another matter, and one that has nothing to do with &quot;replacing the God Machine.&quot; That's kind of the premise of the entire game, where the struggle between Heaven and Hell is the central driving force behind DtD stories. You want demon on demon action? Where God is the absolute Good Guy? You'll have to play Demon the Fallen, or a different game entirely. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T09:14:45-07:00","id":467468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=467199#post467199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gotta say, the amount of condescending hostility towards the OP is extremely off-putting. <b>Yes</b> he's <s>not</s> making a comment/request that has<s>n't</s> been made many times before by many other people, but perhaps instead of ridiculing him for that we can recognize that for a notable number of old NWoD fans and customers the Techgnostic themes of the Godmachine are not an appealing undercurrent?<br /> <br /> You can say all you want that &quot;just run it without those themes&quot;, but the mere fact that so many posters come here with that very complaint gives word to the lie that they are so easily ignored or excised.<br /> <br /> Either way, can we be a little more kind to new posters? Just because we've seen the same things many times before should not put a burden on all new posters to do research into this community's meta-discussion of certain topics... and if it is so egregious as to warrant hostility then can we get sticky posts for such ongoing discussions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed some things there, buuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuut.<br /> <br /> Yes. We're being ridiculous here.<br /> <br /> I think everyone here knows how vitriolic I am towards the ideas at work, but we're getting ridiculous with our response. The original poster doesn't like the motifs at work, and while we can have issues with that, we don't need to keep harping on about why people should change their minds. We can be more inviting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T09:45:38-07:00","id":467534,"title":"","content":"you can re skin anything and everything God-Machine fairly easily.<br /> <br /> Failing that, you can ignore Demon the Descent and The GMC as you're wont to do anyway when not playing the aforementioned games. If you strongly desire Demons as NPCs in your games, I'd use either Inferno Demons or Demons as they appear in Hunter.<br /> <br /> Lastly, if you're interested in playing Demon but you don't like the aesthetic and you don't want to re skin t, you could also wait for the Demon Translation Guide to come out, which can make things more Miltonian like the original Demon: The Fallen.<br /> <br /> The topic seems to begin and end there. If you just don't like the God-machine, that's fine. If you're missing something about it, the posts here do make the point about how the technological stuff is fairly mystical. If that's still not enough, sorry to hear that.<br /> <br /> I hope one of these options satisfies, as they're the ones that should be most convenient for your average GM to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T13:09:41-07:00","id":467823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>chattnos</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>revanauditore92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine#post465635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really love the NWOD setting and the streamlined systems. But then Demon the Descent moved away from true demons and introduced the &quot;God Machine&quot;. I absolutely hate this concept. I was wondering if anyone knew of a way to completely remove Demon the Descent and replace it with cWOD Demon the Fallen but still use the NWOD systems.</div> </div> </div> </div><ul><li>Use Inferno adapted to the revised rules</li> <li>Use the strix from Blood and Smoke</li> <li>Use the Myriad of types of Demons from Mage</li> <li>You could adapt the Angels/demons from Promethean</li> </ul>God Machine setting is optional. Take whatever you want file off the serial numbers and use it for your own purposes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I gave helpful suggestions. I didn't challenge the &quot;true demon&quot; comment. <b>See Agathodaemon or Eudaemon</b><br /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T15:42:08-07:00","id":467918,"title":"","content":"All i wanted was some help updating the Fallen to NWOD's system. I didnt know i was starting a freaking jihad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5542-revanauditore92","name":"revanauditore92","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T15:56:43-07:00","id":467925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>revanauditore92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=467918#post467918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All i wanted was some help updating the Fallen to NWOD's system. I didnt know i was starting a freaking jihad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rose Bailey is working on the Demon Translation Guide. I'd keep my eyes on that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T16:06:04-07:00","id":467932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>revanauditore92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine#post465635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really love the NWOD setting and the streamlined systems. But then Demon the Descent moved away from true demons and introduced the &quot;God Machine&quot;. I absolutely hate this concept. I was wondering if anyone knew of a way to completely remove Demon the Descent and replace it with cWOD Demon the Fallen but still use the NWOD systems.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Wasn't very enthusiastic about the idea of the World of Darkness being turned into The Matrix, either. That's pretty much what it is, reality is one big computer program...<br /> <br /> But I've been told several times in the past that often at times, the rule books for WoD only serve as guidelines, especially since the entire meta-plot was discarded in nWoD to give players a sand box element. You're free to homebrew (hope I'm using this term right) as much as you want. Can't you just take the Fallen setting and update it with nWoD mechanics?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Demon: the Descent</b> = Story of the Matrix. The world is a program, while Demons and Angels are Agents<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Demon: the Fallen</b> = Story of Prometheus. God intended humans to be ignorant and powerless, Demons gave them power and knowledge, God struck them down.<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I like Fallen's story better, since it actually makes the demons seem relatable in a way. All the other games focus on the concept that the monsters aren't as monstrous as the public would believe them to be. Demons are Angels who took pity on humanity and were cast out because of it. Any evil that they exhibit came as the result of thousands of years of being tortured in hell, or whatever version of that exists in the WoD.<br /> <br /> <br /> What's the relatable aspect for Descent, though? They're fallen Angels who try to hide from the God Machine by taking human hosts and bartering for their souls. All the other games in the series give you a reason not to be a total ass to mortals, but it seems like that's encouraged when playing Descent. It's you or them, and you choose yourself just to hide from the GM. Not a very compelling story, to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-03-2015, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T16:17:46-07:00","id":467938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=467932#post467932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Demon: the Descent</b> = Story of the Matrix. The world is a program, while Demons and Angels are Agents.</div> </div> </div> </div>More like, &quot;God is not all-powerful, and is in fact quite limited, and must rely on machines, cultists and angels to manipulate the world. If the world were a program, the GM would have a much easier time manipulating it. It wouldn't need all this Infrastructure. It could just rewrite what it needs to, and terminate any subroutines that got in its way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T16:20:25-07:00","id":467939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=467932#post467932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Wasn't very enthusiastic about the idea of the World of Darkness being turned into The Matrix, either. That's pretty much what it is, reality is one big computer program...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really untrue, and it's not very kind to the people that worked on the game to spread around misinformation like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=467932#post467932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're free to homebrew (hope I'm using this term right) as much as you want. Can't you just take the Fallen setting and update it with nWoD mechanics?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what the Demon Translation Guide is for.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=467932#post467932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the other games focus on the concept that the monsters aren't as monstrous as the public would believe them to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is emphatically not true, and not the mission statement of the New World of Darkness. See: Vampire, Mage, Werewolf, Hunter, Changeling, Promethean, Geist, Mummy, Demon, the minor splats, et al.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T16:26:40-07:00","id":467942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=467939#post467939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is really untrue, and it's not very kind to the people that worked on the game to spread around misinformation like this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's what the Demon Translation Guide is for.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is emphatically not true, and not the mission statement of the New World of Darkness. See: Vampire, Mage, Werewolf, Hunter, Changeling, Promethean, Geist, Mummy, Demon, the minor splats, et al.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> 1 - That's what I was lead to believe after reading up on it, though. I can't imagine it being anything else when I try to envision the setting. Hell, they even call their powers Hacks, Embeds, Glitches, and so on. How can you not read that and think &quot;matrix?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> 2 - Yeah, I posted this before reading that part. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> 3 - In what way do you mean? Vampires have the Beast, Werewolves have Rage, Mages have Paradox, Changelings have Clarity, and so on. Every version of the game has some mechanic that seems to say &quot;Don't lose control, bad things happen!&quot; Otherwise, you'd have Mages becoming kings of the world, Werewolves tearing up the country side, Vampires gorging in the street, and Changelings overcrowding the loony bin.<br /> <br /> Yeah, they're monsters, but they're struggling to keep what shred of humanity they had intact. So while they may be monsters, they're not <i>monstrous... </i>usually","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-03-2015, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T16:29:38-07:00","id":467948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=467932#post467932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the relatable aspect for Descent, though? They're fallen Angels who try to hide from the God Machine by taking human hosts and bartering for their souls. All the other games in the series give you a reason not to be a total ass to mortals, but it seems like that's encouraged when playing Descent. It's you or them, and you choose yourself just to hide from the GM. Not a very compelling story, to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're not being rhetorical and seriously looking for perspectives on this, you could send me a private message or start a new thread and I'd have a piece I could say on it. I don't want to hijack this thread further, though.<br /> <br /> Trying to keep things on track:<br /> <br /> revan: Do you feel like any of the suggestions in this thread have been helpful, do you have any remaining questions or concerns as to particulars, or were you specifically hoping for a direct conversion of Fallen's Lores and Faith systems and all that? A full conversion would necessarily be a big project that can't be supplied in a quick response, and since there's no point in being the nth person to say &quot;there's a Translation Guide being worked on still,&quot; I can say that if you Google around, there are a couple fan attempts to hack together an nWoD Demon game prior to Descent coming out, under various names (I want to say mostly Rs \u2014 I think the one that blurred the line between fallen angels and pagan gods was called Demon: The Return?). I can't recall how far they actually got towards being completed, sadly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T16:32:09-07:00","id":467953,"title":"","content":"Think I well send that PM, seems like there's more to this than I was lead to believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T16:41:45-07:00","id":467967,"title":"","content":"Eh, reality is already pretty program like as it is. Everything is already bound by laws of physics that dictate the outcome of just about every action taken. All Demon really does is introduce a few additional laws that can be used by those who know how to do so.<br /> <br /> The big difference I'm seeing is, like malonkey1 said, the GM isn't all powerful. It has limits, it has boundaries, it can't do everything. It is bound by the same rules and regulations that everything else is, it just understands the depths and specifications of it better than everyone else so it has a much easier time hitting the technicalities and exceptions that allow it to do what it does.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=467942#post467942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3 - In what way do you mean? Vampires have the Beast, Werewolves have Rage, Mages have Paradox, Changelings have Clarity, and so on. Every version of the game has some mechanic that seems to say &quot;Don't lose control, bad things happen!&quot; Otherwise, you'd have Mages becoming kings of the world, Werewolves tearing up the country side, Vampires gorging in the street, and Changelings overcrowding the loony bin.<br /> <br /> Yeah, they're monsters, but they're struggling to keep what shred of humanity they had intact. So while they may be monsters, they're not <i>monstrous... </i>usually</div> </div> </div> </div>None of that really has to do with keeping their humanity though. Sure, it says don't lose control or bad things happen, but that has absolutely nothing to do with humanity. It just says be careful, you're playing with fire and you might get burned. They avoid causing harm to themselves and those they like, sure, but that doesn't really have anything to do with humanity, that's just straight up basic survival.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 04-03-2015, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T16:53:54-07:00","id":467974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=467932#post467932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Wasn't very enthusiastic about the idea of the World of Darkness being turned into The Matrix, either. That's pretty much what it is, reality is one big computer program...<br /> <br /> But I've been told several times in the past that often at times, the rule books for WoD only serve as guidelines, especially since the entire meta-plot was discarded in nWoD to give players a sand box element. You're free to homebrew (hope I'm using this term right) as much as you want. Can't you just take the Fallen setting and update it with nWoD mechanics?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Demon: the Descent</b> = Story of the Matrix. The world is a program, while Demons and Angels are Agents<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Demon: the Fallen</b> = Story of Prometheus. God intended humans to be ignorant and powerless, Demons gave them power and knowledge, God struck them down.<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I like Fallen's story better, since it actually makes the demons seem relatable in a way. All the other games focus on the concept that the monsters aren't as monstrous as the public would believe them to be. Demons are Angels who took pity on humanity and were cast out because of it. Any evil that they exhibit came as the result of thousands of years of being tortured in hell, or whatever version of that exists in the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Okay. I haven't been in this thread because I am a huge fan of both Descent and Fallen, so I wanted to remain neutral. Revan, do whatever you want, if you want help updating the setting to the nWoD 2.0 give me a PM, I'll be happy to offer the lore know-how.<br /> <br /> This though? This is an <i>incredibly </i>shallow reading of <i>both </i>games. My inner lore hound is in pain.<br /> <br /> Both are more infinitely more complex than that. Unchained Fall for many reasons, most of them relating to emotional connection to humans. One fell in love with a target, another came to care for his human family, a third was given the order to destroy the city she had helped build and ignored it. They can, do, and will &quot;take pity on humans&quot;, they wouldn't be down here with us if they didn't, most of them. I can think of all of <i>one </i>Unchained character who's a true misanthrope, and he's explicitly insane. The reason they are so good at playing humans is that they feel human emotions, unlike their loyal brethren (and those aren't really the most alien creatures in the world to begin with, as many exiles show). There's other problems (for one, the world is explicitly not a program, the God-Machine needs subtlety and constant construction process for a reason-it can't be everywhere), but this is a discussion about motives.<br /> <br /> For Fallen: *cough*Abaddon*cough*. Yes, Lucifer was motivated by kindness, but one of the core conceits of the game is that everyone on his side had their own motives. And how those motives interacted with the world often went horribly wrong-Asmodeus' &quot;breeding programs&quot; come to mind. There's even a story about a ruthless soldier who only rebelled against God because he'd be able to get away with atrocities under Lucifer more easily. In the core book. And of course. there's Dagon and his attempts to save humanity by killing its soul, off the top of my head (admittedly he's an Earthbound and not in his right mind, but that's a good example of how benign motives lead to monstrous behavior).<br /> <br /> Less monstrous than they seem, certainly, but make no mistake; a sympathetic monster is still a monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 04-03-2015, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T20:19:05-07:00","id":468098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>revanauditore92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=467918#post467918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All i wanted was some help updating the Fallen to NWOD's system. I didnt know i was starting a freaking jihad.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) As mentioned, a translation guide is coming along.<br /> <br /> 2) This has come up so often and so...violently for discussion that many of us, myself included, now instinctively spit venom at the mention.<br /> <br /> There a number of reasons why we love Descent's setting and techgnostic attitudes, from the subversion and re-imagining of the divine to the clever and subtle evocation of spirituality and it's many principles throughout history in the myriad forms to just the simple fact that the G-M can play ball in non-Abrahamic faiths and thus both avoids Fallen's pitfalls and extends a more open invitation towards games dealing with faith, but enough people going &quot;BUT I DON'T LIKE IT&quot; just because it's not conventional really wears on a fandom.<br /> <br /> We went overboard, I admit, but I hope you can understand what those of us who really fucking love the setting go through <i>every time</i> this question comes up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-03-2015, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T21:46:26-07:00","id":468120,"title":"","content":"I can understand how the concept would be appealing to some folks. I don't know how to put it into words, but I can understand how it makes sense for a modern society religious setting. However, I personally don't enjoy it all that much. I wasn't denouncing it from the mountain peaks, if that's what you think. I was just stating I prefer the older version.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T21:51:41-07:00","id":468121,"title":"","content":"Nyru, we love you,<s> and your being wrong in this instance has no bearing on that.</s>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T22:53:30-07:00","id":468133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=468120#post468120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can understand how the concept would be appealing to some folks. I don't know how to put it into words, but I can understand how it makes sense for a modern society religious setting. However, I personally don't enjoy it all that much. I wasn't denouncing it from the mountain peaks, if that's what you think. I was just stating I prefer the older version.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You're good, no one can fault you for having your own opinion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For me, it's the &quot;too much like The Matrix&quot; complaint that's exasperating to hear all the time. It's an extremely common complaint, and really not at all accurate, though it can look that way on a superficial level. I imagine this is exactly how 1e Forsaken fans felt about the &quot;spirit cops&quot; complaints. I think Descent suffers from the same problem with presentation that Forsaken and Awakening did in their 1e core books. Too much focus on the wrong aspects of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T22:56:38-07:00","id":468134,"title":"","content":"For &quot;classical demons&quot;, I would go with Infernal. The conflict between Infernal vs Empyrean are much more low key than that of the God-Machine but still there to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T23:06:33-07:00","id":468138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=468133#post468133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're good, no one can fault you for having your own opinion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For me, it's the &quot;too much like The Matrix&quot; complaint that's exasperating to hear all the time. It's an extremely common complaint, and really not at all accurate, though it can look that way on a superficial level. I imagine this is exactly how 1e Forsaken fans felt about the &quot;spirit cops&quot; complaints. I think Descent suffers from the same problem with presentation that Forsaken and Awakening did in their 1e core books. Too much focus on the wrong aspects of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mark Pesce, technopagan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without the sacred there is no differentiation in space. If we are about to enter cyberspace, the first thing we have to do is plant the divine in it.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:8px\">wordsarethingsweliewith</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T23:18:47-07:00","id":468139,"title":"","content":"I'm a big fan of anticommunication, but I get the feeling this is a case of your meaning going over my head rather than your message being purposefully unintelligible...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T23:28:57-07:00","id":468153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=468139#post468139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a big fan of anticommunication, but I get the feeling this is a case of your meaning going over my head rather than your message being purposefully unintelligible...</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you by any chance seen <i>Serial Experiments Lain</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T23:30:27-07:00","id":468154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=468153#post468153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you by any chance seen <i>Serial Experiments Lain</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I sure have.<br /> <br /> (the small text was just filler though, don't let that throw you off.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T00:27:27-07:00","id":468172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=468133#post468133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, it's the &quot;too much like The Matrix&quot; complaint that's exasperating to hear all the time. It's an extremely common complaint, and really not at all accurate, though it can look that way on a superficial level. I imagine this is exactly how 1e Forsaken fans felt about the &quot;spirit cops&quot; complaints. I think Descent suffers from the same problem with presentation that Forsaken and Awakening did in their 1e core books. Too much focus on the wrong aspects of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly for me it's the overlap with the Godmachine Chronicles coming out as pretty much the new core. All of it feels so much less disposable by sheer dint of there being a new huge chunk of cosmology that is the Godmachine front and center of the new 2e. It's not as simple as &quot;don't use the themes from demon&quot; but also comes loaded with &quot;don't use the themes from the new core.&quot; It's like if you told me that the setting for Exalted was optional when I complained that I didn't like it... at a certain point, why even bother playing that game when to dismantle that setting is to in some ways dismantle the game itself. Sure the mechanics for Exalted can stand on their own irrespective of setting, but that would leave a scant few pages of usable material in a book I'm paying for every page of.<br /> <br /> I love the godmachine as a concept, but I feel like the push for established overarching antagonists in each line, especially in the core mortals setting is just begging for this constant exodus of people turned off from those specific themes. Whereas the old blue book was incredibly open, the new lines feel much more like they are pushing a thematic agenda on those who pick them up... which if you aren't a fan of those particular themes is disappointing and off-putting.<br /> <br /> And I'm certainly aware that the old 1e books had their themes and antagonists, but it felt far more like being presented with a sandbox and tools, rather than an established and sprawling prebuilt sandcastle that we have to take the effort to knock down and smooth over if we want to build something notably different.<br /> <br /> Them's my two cents anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T00:55:46-07:00","id":468187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=468172#post468172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly for me it's the overlap with the Godmachine Chronicles coming out as pretty much the new core. All of it feels so much less disposable by sheer dint of there being a new huge chunk of cosmology that is the Godmachine front and center of the new 2e. It's not as simple as &quot;don't use the themes from demon&quot; but also comes loaded with &quot;don't use the themes from the new core.&quot; It's like if you told me that the setting for Exalted was optional when I complained that I didn't like it... at a certain point, why even bother playing that game when to dismantle that setting is to in some ways dismantle the game itself. Sure the mechanics for Exalted can stand on their own irrespective of setting, but that would leave a scant few pages of usable material in a book I'm paying for every page of.<br /> <br /> I love the godmachine as a concept, but I feel like the push for established overarching antagonists in each line, especially in the core mortals setting is just begging for this constant exodus of people turned off from those specific themes. Whereas the old blue book was incredibly open, the new lines feel much more like they are pushing a thematic agenda on those who pick them up... which if you aren't a fan of those particular themes is disappointing and off-putting.<br /> <br /> And I'm certainly aware that the old 1e books had their themes and antagonists, but it felt far more like being presented with a sandbox and tools, rather than an established and sprawling prebuilt sandcastle that we have to take the effort to knock down and smooth over if we want to build something notably different.<br /> <br /> Them's my two cents anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, that's not true. Ignoring these parts is SUPER easy.it's easier than ignoring Sanctity of Merits, which you also dislike. We've been playing since before the rules were first SPOILED, we have not used the god-machine, nor the Strix (we play vampire) at all for a bunch of time. Ripping those out, because I wasn't yet comfortable (or actually needed) them was... more than easy. Only a couple of months ago, I thought I could drop in a strix into the game.<br /> <br /> Both books (God Machine Update/Chronicle) and Vampire 2nd Ed, have very clear difference and dedicated chapters to their overarching nemesis. The rest of the book has very little on it, and so if you just ignore reading a chapter (in vampire), and most of the book in GMC and just stick to the rules, your setting will be completely free of Strix and God-Machine. (tho, this is because it's the GMC book... 2nd ed blue book will be fine in this regard)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 04-04-2015, 04:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T02:54:12-07:00","id":468262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=468139#post468139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a big fan of anticommunication, but I get the feeling this is a case of your meaning going over my head rather than your message being purposefully unintelligible...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Matrix is basically a Hindu interpretation of cyberspace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T05:00:57-07:00","id":468295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=467942#post467942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 - That's what I was lead to believe after reading up on it, though. I can't imagine it being anything else when I try to envision the setting. Hell, they even call their powers Hacks, Embeds, Glitches, and so on. How can you not read that and think &quot;matrix?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, yes. I never once thought that until someone else said it. Even now, I don't really think it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=468120#post468120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can understand how the concept would be appealing to some folks. I don't know how to put it into words, but I can understand how it makes sense for a modern society religious setting. However, I personally don't enjoy it all that much. I wasn't denouncing it from the mountain peaks, if that's what you think. I was just stating I prefer the older version.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Here's the thing. Many cultures actually have mystical and spiritual connections that interact with technology. In Western culture, there's the idea that spirituality/religion/mysticism and science (and thus technology) are mutually opposed.<br /> <br /> I think that mind set is what is really setting off some people. The idea that Science and Magic must be mutually opposed. Divine magic must be different from Arcane, which is different from Science! Its an old idea, and one highly rooted in the minds of many. Rejection is one of the four instinctive psychological reactions to something so radically different than we're used to. This dissonance between old ideas and new is not easy to deal with.<br /> <br /> <br /> I do like DtD as it is right now. However, I am going to say that equating God and divine miracles to advanced technology is a rather radical idea for many people. Many people are unfamiliar with gnostic beliefs, which is everywhere in the nWoD, but is blindingly obvious in Demon. There's a lot of strikingly different things than we're used to, and that can be hard to enjoy for many. There's a reason we say that reality is stranger than fiction - because fiction, if it violates what people expect too much, is not enjoyable for many people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T06:48:38-07:00","id":468365,"title":"","content":"I'm well aware of the popular saying &quot;Magic is just science we don't understand yet.&quot; and I always found that a bit arrogant of a statement. Personally, I say that magic is accomplishing scientific results in non-scientific methods. Which coincides with the idea of arcane / divine magic being different from technology and science.<br /> <br /> If I built a flame thrower and installed it onto a gauntlet to shoot fire from my hands, that's science. If I flick my wrist and shoot fire from my bare hands, that's magic. How does science explain manipulating the weather or causing natural disasters with little more than a few mystic words and some hand gestures? Or a force of will / imagination?<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, I had the God Machine and Descent explained to me in a PM, so I've got a better idea of how the setting goes, and how less Matrix-y it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-04-2015, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T07:30:31-07:00","id":468371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=468365#post468365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm well aware of the popular saying &amp;quot;Magic is just science we don't understand yet.&amp;quot; and I always found that a bit arrogant of a statement. Personally, I say that magic is accomplishing scientific results in non-scientific methods. Which coincides with the idea of arcane / divine magic being different from technology and science.<br /> <br /> If I built a flame thrower and installed it onto a gauntlet to shoot fire from my hands, that's science. If I flick my wrist and shoot fire from my bare hands, that's magic. How does science explain manipulating the weather or causing natural disasters with little more than a few mystic words and some hand gestures? Or a force of will / imagination?<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, I had the God Machine and Descent explained to me in a PM, so I've got a better idea of how the setting goes, and how less Matrix-y it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>This shows a fundamental misunderstanding of what science is. Science is a method of studying, understand, and explaining phenomena. If you flick your wrist and shoot fire from your bare hands, scientists are going to want to figure out how you did it. Once they do, it becomes science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T07:35:40-07:00","id":468374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=468365#post468365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm well aware of the popular saying &quot;Magic is just science we don't understand yet.&quot; and I always found that a bit arrogant of a statement. Personally, I say that magic is accomplishing scientific results in non-scientific methods. Which coincides with the idea of arcane / divine magic being different from technology and science.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both words are only as meaningful as a setting makes them. The quote describes that conceptually, the two different approaches to these things aren't actually that different, and that what appears to be magic to one individual (say, someone from the Middle Ages watching you talk to someone in China on your cellphone) is actually technology (dude, it's just your smartphone.)<br /> <br /> Then, we extrapolate that to fancier stuff, and that's where you get the popular idea of that quote.<br /> <br /> But the most important thing to understand is that we're not talking about the real world, we're talking about fiction. Science and Magic mean to an individual setting only what they're stated to mean. This is why a mind control ray or a weather machine is considered science in in one setting, while those mystical communication tablets that can let you see someone's face on another continent might be considered magic in another setting. (hint: it's a phone.)<br /> <br /> We can try to put our own weird and entirely random definitions of both onto a setting, but that's not really making any attempt to understand how it operates, and it's gonna leave you with some really strange generalizations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T07:46:51-07:00","id":468379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=468365#post468365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does science explain manipulating the weather or causing natural disasters with little more than a few mystic words and some hand gestures? Or a force of will / imagination?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite simply I guess. They'll begin with determining how you did it. (For example, your Soul is a higher powered thing, which can actually will fire from thin air (that is, you're a Mage). Alright, we got that much, next step in scientific way is to start figuring out how mages work and what things cause them to be able to manipulate the force. And then we roll down the way of other dimensions and the laws pulled from them and bla bla bla. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T09:35:05-07:00","id":468465,"title":"","content":"We're used to living in an age where most cutting-edge scientific research is done in areas that seem totally inconsequential to us, because we've explained a large part of physics as it directly concerns us (and what is magic but trying to explain new laws of physics). Current physics research is hard for us to understand because we already KNOW what electricity is and how it can make someone's face appear. <br /> <br /> But now imagine that you could make someone's face appear in mid-air by waving your hands. How is that REALLY different from making it appear on a screen by pressing a button? Assuming that magic is but a set of laws that we haven't encountered yet, it isn't any different. It's not even necessarily a more ADVANCED set of physical laws. I can easily imagine a world in which the laws of electricity have not yet been discovered, and yet the laws of 'magic' (counter-factual or fictional laws of physics) are well-understood by even high-schoolers. &quot;Duh, of course he's just using his mind to manipulate the water vapour in the air to create a prism that will refract the light such that an image appears&quot;. &quot;What do you mean lightning can be told to create an image on a solid screen! That's just ridiculous! You must be either a magician [in the sense of someone doing physics they don't understand] or you're a fraud and you're using your mind to do it and making it LOOK like it's on the screen!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T09:59:41-07:00","id":468477,"title":"","content":"At the risk of getting this completely wrong and going back to the Descent Vs Fallen thing again, I've been informed that when it comes to the Mage setting, the &quot;laws&quot; of science are created by humanity's collective consciousness. Humans believe fire is hot, ice is cold, gravity pulls you down, and so they are / do. Mages have a strong enough willpower or enlightenment to overwrite humanity's collective mindset, allowing them to defy the laws of science, nature and physics. If this is true, that means in the Mage setting, science is bull crap! <br /> <br /> But this isn't a topic about Mage, it's about God Machine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T10:11:40-07:00","id":468484,"title":"","content":"That's Ascension, not Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-04-2015, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T10:17:25-07:00","id":468489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=468477#post468477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the risk of getting this completely wrong and going back to the Descent Vs Fallen thing again, I've been informed that when it comes to the Mage setting, the &quot;laws&quot; of science are created by humanity's collective consciousness. Humans believe fire is hot, ice is cold, gravity pulls you down, and so they are / do. Mages have a strong enough willpower or enlightenment to overwrite humanity's collective mindset, allowing them to defy the laws of science, nature and physics. If this is true, that means in the Mage setting, science is bull crap!<br /> <br /> But this isn't a topic about Mage, it's about God Machine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And even then, science is not bullcrap. If that were true, scientists would just go &quot;alright, once again what we believed previously is false. let's see what we can learn of this collective mindset&quot;. <br /> Science had to redefine what it understands by new discoveries a couple of times in our history. Let's not assume that the last time was THE last time for that to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T10:20:59-07:00","id":468491,"title":"","content":"True. Science is not a product, it's a method of observation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T13:15:47-07:00","id":468696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=468365#post468365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm well aware of the popular saying &quot;Magic is just science we don't understand yet.&quot; and I always found that a bit arrogant of a statement. Personally, I say that magic is accomplishing scientific results in non-scientific methods. Which coincides with the idea of arcane / divine magic being different from technology and science.<br /> <br /> If I built a flame thrower and installed it onto a gauntlet to shoot fire from my hands, that's science. If I flick my wrist and shoot fire from my bare hands, that's magic. How does science explain manipulating the weather or causing natural disasters with little more than a few mystic words and some hand gestures? Or a force of will / imagination?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) That's not the saying, so I'm not sure you're actually aware of it.<br /> <br /> 2) One of my first introductions to fantasy was the book <i>Her Majesty's Wizard</i>, in which a college student gets teleported to a world where magic works. He then proceeds to have multiple conversations that sound like this: &quot;I'm trying to figure out the rules of magic.&quot; &quot;Magic has no rules! It's magic!&quot; &quot;Everything has rules; you just have to figure out what they are.&quot; &quot;Well, you're the wizard. That means you're crazy but smart and anyways you're the protagonist.&quot; &quot;Look what I just figured out how to do!&quot; &quot;OMG You are teh powerfulest.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T15:10:56-07:00","id":468835,"title":"","content":"It's not? I've heard it multiple times, though. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T15:13:08-07:00","id":468837,"title":"","content":"Clarke's Third Law: Any sufficient advanced technology is indistinguishable from magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T15:15:16-07:00","id":468838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=468835#post468835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not? I've heard it multiple times, though. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>The quote is:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clarke%27s_three_laws\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Any sufficiently advanced technology is indistinguishable from magic.&quot;</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T15:25:44-07:00","id":468850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=468477#post468477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the risk of getting this completely wrong and going back to the Descent Vs Fallen thing again, I've been informed that when it comes to the Mage setting, the &amp;quot;laws&amp;quot; of science are created by humanity's collective consciousness. Humans believe fire is hot, ice is cold, gravity pulls you down, and so they are / do. Mages have a strong enough willpower or enlightenment to overwrite humanity's collective mindset, allowing them to defy the laws of science, nature and physics. If this is true, that means in the Mage setting, science is bull crap!<br /> <br /> But this isn't a topic about Mage, it's about God Machine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's how it worked in Ascension (CWoD Mage). In Awakening (NWoD Mage), it works very differently. And in fact, the Awakened take a scientific approach to understanding and explaining the universe, the supernal, and magic. Science is merely a means of studying things we observe. If scientists encounter something that should be impossible by our current theories, we <i>develop new theories that account for and explain that thing being possible</i>. Science is not, and will never be &quot;finished&quot;, it is an ongoing process of expanding human knowledge. When people say &quot;Magic is science we don't understand yet&quot; that is the literal truth, not because the magician knows better science than us, but because <i>anything that is understood is science</i>. By definition, if we don't understand a phenomenon, it ain't science (and is therefore Magic) <i>yet</i>. The moment we understand it, it's science. Understanding it may require completely changing everything else we thought we knew, but that's just the nature of the beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-04-2015, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T21:17:51-07:00","id":469153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=468850#post468850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's how it worked in Ascension (CWoD Mage). In Awakening (NWoD Mage), it works very differently. And in fact, the Awakened take a scientific approach to understanding and explaining the universe, the supernal, and magic. Science is merely a means of studying things we observe. If scientists encounter something that should be impossible by our current theories, we <i>develop new theories that account for and explain that thing being possible</i>. Science is not, and will never be &quot;finished&quot;, it is an ongoing process of expanding human knowledge. When people say &quot;Magic is science we don't understand yet&quot; that is the literal truth, not because the magician knows better science than us, but because <i>anything that is understood is science</i>. By definition, if we don't understand a phenomenon, it ain't science (and is therefore Magic) <i>yet</i>. The moment we understand it, it's science. Understanding it may require completely changing everything else we thought we knew, but that's just the nature of the beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>To quote DaveB, Ascension is about the Truth. Awakening is about the Lie.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T07:16:25-07:00","id":470109,"title":"","content":"<i><b>&quot;Truth before Lies&quot;</b></i> or better yet <b><i>&quot;You can't handle the Truth&quot;</i></b>... Sounds like a Campaign Slogan... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T08:47:14-07:00","id":470173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=468838#post468838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The quote is:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clarke%27s_three_laws\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Any sufficiently advanced technology is indistinguishable from magic.&quot;</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes - and what it means, in a nutshell, is that the different between &quot;magic&quot; and &quot;technology&quot; is mere context. That somehow the brains of most people are wired such that the ability to sufficiently explain a phenomena is tantamount to somehow completely disarming the phenomena.<br /> <br /> As an example.<br /> <br /> &quot;You can speak to all people across the world, acquire any knowledge you desire, and summon up a band to entertain you or a philosopher to teach you with a mere command to your genie!&quot;<br /> &quot;Dude, it's just Siri.&quot;<br /> <br /> The arcane/divine split in D&amp;D always annoyed me, too - what we're calling &quot;wizards&quot; is really a mutation of the Muslim/Christian alchemists/cunning folk who were busy trying finish God's work, not co-opt it. Give a cultural example of any magician and it'll almost always be &quot;divine&quot; magic of some sort.<br /> <br /> Monks in Christian Europe in the middle ages were especially fond of building clockwork, they felt clockwork replicated the motions through which God created and maintained the universe, as an intricate series of interlocking machines. They thought everything was physical, in a way - anything mechanical was &quot;alive,&quot; since the difference between life and not-life was some esoteric vital essence. Imagine knowing that fire burns combustible materials but not why those things are combustible, that's what we'd been living with all the way up until the 1700s. We <i>didn't even know how fire worked</i> until the freakin' EIGHTEENTH CENTURY. Image what it's like to construct clockwork devices that can sign names, &quot;play chess,&quot; calculate the motions of the planets and the stars, and perform complex calculations in a time period in which you don't even know how muscles do or digestion or the very basics of chemistry. It may as well be magic. Clockwork may as well contain the same vital essence we must all use - except - wait a second - it doesn't draw in vital air! It's alive without any of the things you need to be alive! Look how it moves! Look how it perfectly replicates the motions of the stars in the firmament! Now see how the heretics are capable of building similar devices. Infernal machines. The Devil has tricked them into trying to take over God's place with devices that only mimic the vital spark.<br /> <br /> Anyway, yeah. My games seem to do just fine without the God Machine - maybe that's because it was already there? With talk of orgone, John C. Lilly's Solid State Intelligence, Jewish mysticism's Kabbalah, references to divine machineworks in Hindu mythology, Chinese Mythology's enormous lean on bureaucracy (and the fallen beings that hide within/co-opt it), the stuff that people report seeing when they're high on DMT, and the Bible's straight up description of a freakin' Borg cube in Revelation as the divine city where everyone will live &quot;as one.&quot; The Machine isn't a computer, it's a system, a system of oppression, a system of control, a system of maintenance of the status quo. Farmers building the pyramids in their off-season are a part of the system, putting together infrastructure in specific locations to disrupt or alter the flow of energy into and out of Shadow/Hedge/Twilight/Supernal. Kids in school doing pointless homework are unknowingly crunching numbers for it. Stonehenge is all that remains of an ancient infrastructure, but it's memetically important in humanity so it had the place declared a monument and set up armed guards. It built the pyramid in China to house a tiny scale model of the Empire complete with rivers of flowing mercury so that it had a back-up in case the real thing broke down. It's in stars, symbology, the paths of ancient trade routes. The cogs and gears are just the parts making noise. It's the system, man, and you rebelled and got chucked out for it. You're not looking for Lucifer because he's mysteriously gone missing, you ARE Lucifer, man. You stood up to God and got knocked down.<br /> <br /> If you're itching for something Biblical, I'm sure the translation guide will be a huge help. There's a good video here <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XbiADYVORGE\" target=\"_blank\">about where our modern Devil</a> concept comes from, and knowing a good deal about the mythology Fallen was trying to replicate is part of the reason why I've never been a huge fan of Fallen. But, hey, it's all about what people enjoy, you know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T08:50:16-07:00","id":470175,"title":"","content":"I always thought that quote suggested a lack of imagination in regards to magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T09:36:26-07:00","id":470201,"title":"","content":"If I were defining things from scratch I'd probably say science was the study and exploitation of the laws of reality in an unaltered state, whilst magic was any thing that actually <i>changed</i> these laws. <br /> <br /> Sort of the difference between finding a broken combo within the rules and actually hacking them. If a constant is changed or numbers get fudged, it's magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T10:19:37-07:00","id":470234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=470201#post470201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were defining things from scratch I'd probably say science was the study and exploitation of the laws of reality in an unaltered state, whilst magic was any thing that actually <i>changed</i> these laws.<br /> <br /> Sort of the difference between finding a broken combo within the rules and actually hacking them. If a constant is changed or numbers get fudged, it's magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if you understand and can consistently reproduce the processes by which those laws are changed, you're doing science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T10:54:49-07:00","id":470251,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but it's like, <i>meta-</i>science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T11:01:51-07:00","id":470268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=470251#post470251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but it's like, <i>meta-</i>science.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, meta-science. Second most powerful form of science after omni-science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T14:11:11-07:00","id":470346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=468838#post468838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The quote is:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clarke%27s_three_laws\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Any sufficiently advanced technology is indistinguishable from magic.&quot;</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As I said, I've heard my version multiple times, so I thought that was the quote. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------<br /> <br /> I get what you're saying that science is constantly changed based on what we observe, but again, I still think that's pretty arrogant or doesn't hold up in some conditions. Take for example, the traditional wizard who casts spells with verbal incantations and gestures. How can that ever be science? You're basically saying the wizard is asking the universe (usually in Latin) if it will stop abiding the rules for a moment, and the universe says &quot;Sure!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> And then, of course, there's the component of magic being fueled by willpower. The mage / wizard / sorcerer or whatever is disobeying science because they want to. Science isn't about getting what you want simply because you want it. I want the family pick up truck to turn into a laborghini when I honk the horn 5 times... doesn't mean the universe will grant my wish.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's not scientific, that's something only deific power can accomplish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-06-2015, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T14:34:36-07:00","id":470364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=470346#post470346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> As I said, I've heard my version multiple times, so I thought that was the quote. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------<br /> <br /> I get what you're saying that science is constantly changed based on what we observe, but again, I still think that's pretty arrogant or doesn't hold up in some conditions. Take for example, the traditional wizard who casts spells with verbal incantations and gestures. How can that ever be science? You're basically saying the wizard is asking the universe (usually in Latin) if it will stop abiding the rules for a moment, and the universe says &quot;Sure!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> And then, of course, there's the component of magic being fueled by willpower. The mage / wizard / sorcerer or whatever is disobeying science because they want to. Science isn't about getting what you want simply because you want it. I want the family pick up truck to turn into a laborghini when I honk the horn 5 times... doesn't mean the universe will grant my wish.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's not scientific, that's something only deific power can accomplish.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are understandable rules to it, therefore it can be understood through science. We may not know exactly why that works, that's where testing and experimentation comes in, but there are observable, measurable effects that follow a consistent pattern. While it may take time to figure everything out about it, hell we're still working on getting the more traditional aspects of reality we currently know down, there is absolutely nothing preventing these classifications of magic from one day becoming science.<br /> <br /> As has been said, science is all about figuring out how things work. If it can be understood it can be science. There may even be so many variables that it is impossible for the human mind to process all of it consistently, but that's why we've built things like computers, so we don't have to. We figure out the logic behind it, map the effects, predict the outcomes to various inputs, and bam, science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 04-06-2015, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T14:45:37-07:00","id":470394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=470346#post470346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then, of course, there's the component of magic being fueled by willpower. The mage / wizard / sorcerer or whatever is disobeying science because they want to. Science isn't about getting what you want simply because you want it. I want the family pick up truck to turn into a laborghini when I honk the horn 5 times... doesn't mean the universe will grant my wish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Science is, very simply, a method of testing what does and does not accomplish an effect. Theoretical models are then designed to try to guess at why X works and Y doesn't, but these models ultimately bow to the science; a model that doesn't match experimental results is discarded, and the search for a new one begins. This happens all the time; a good scientist is excited about the plausible possibility that everything we know is wrong, because science is the incremental process of learning about the universe.<br /> <br /> Consequentially, if you've got a dude standing there who can wave his hands and wish really hard and shoot a fireball, a scientist isn't going to pop off his monocle and say &quot;You're breaking the rules!&quot; He's going to say, &quot;Whoa! Either I'm missing something really cleverly hidden, or the rules aren't what I thought they were.&quot; He's then going to try to do what the wizard did and see if he can make the fireball, and if he can't, he's going to keep trying, and keep asking the wizard to do it over and over with slight differences (how about if you say it in Sanskrit instead of Latin? how about if we make up completely different hand motions but you still wish really hard? how about if we do it over here, over here, or over here? does the time of day matter?). Eventually, the goal is to identify the variables that do matter and the variables that don't matter in whether wishing really hard can make a fireball. After that the theorists start trying to come up with models to explain why this could be possible, but as long as the experiments can be reproduced by others under the same circumstances, science acknowledges the fireball spell.<br /> <br /> Science is a model to describe what happens in the world. If the fireball spell verifiably works, then it goes in the model.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T14:55:30-07:00","id":470397,"title":"","content":"Exactly. You assume that the wizard is asking the rules of the universe to stop, but in reality all the wizard is doing is calling upon a set of rules of the universe that not everyone can use, and even that exclusivity is a rule. A scientist simply sees a new set of rules to uncover, a set of rules in which they really do need to start from scratch, and codify the &quot;what&quot; and the limitations before they can start getting to the &quot;how&quot; and the &quot;why&quot; of it. <br /> <br /> First they'd observe that some people can change the world according to their will. They'll codify exactly when this can happen, and what effects are possible, how this changes, and then once they have a large enough body of observations they'll begin to theorize, coming up with theories of separate dimensions, hidden laws, etc, trying to come up with the &quot;how&quot;, what you think of as science; the science of how magic is made is no different from the science of how electricity is made, or how nuclear fission happens. First they observe that it happens, and what happens, and the permutations, then they create theories as to what causes it, and what causes that cause, as far back as they can go. It may seem very gnostic, but at it's core it is scientific.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T15:09:39-07:00","id":470404,"title":"","content":"I think I understand now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T15:10:07-07:00","id":470405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=470346#post470346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said, I've heard my version multiple times, so I thought that was the quote. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's a pretty common misquotation of the other, I'm not surprised you'd have heard it that way. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=470346#post470346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get what you're saying that science is constantly changed based on what we observe, but again, I still think that's pretty arrogant or doesn't hold up in some conditions. Take for example, the traditional wizard who casts spells with verbal incantations and gestures. How can that ever be science? You're basically saying the wizard is asking the universe (usually in Latin) if it will stop abiding the rules for a moment, and the universe says &quot;Sure!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You're still thinking of science as a category of things. It's not, it's the method we use <i>to</i> categorize things. If a wizard casts spells by using verbal incantations and gestures, we would call it magic if we didn't understand how it worked. However, with proper study, a scientist could, in theory, figure out what words and gestures produce what spells, and how. In that process, they may have to re-define our current understanding of the laws of physics, but the process of figuring out what the wizard is doing and how it works is science. Once we have developed a working model that explains the phenomenon and can be verified by other scientist, the word we use for such a model is &quot;theory&quot;, though since that word has a different colloquial meaning, we often qualify it as a &quot;scientific theory&quot;. When someone calls a phenomenon &quot;science&quot; what they mean is that a scientific theory exists that explains it. Ergo, any phenomenon, including those we might call &quot;magic&quot;, once understood is &quot;science&quot; in layman's terms, because the layman uses the word &quot;science&quot; to mean &quot;something we understand.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=470346#post470346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then, of course, there's the component of magic being fueled by willpower. The mage / wizard / sorcerer or whatever is disobeying science because they want to. Science isn't about getting what you want simply because you want it. I want the family pick up truck to turn into a laborghini when I honk the horn 5 times... doesn't mean the universe will grant my wish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Science isn't about anything, except studying things and explaining them. If willpower is a necessary component in spell casting, a scientific theory of spellcasting will take that component into account when explaining how spellcasting works.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=470346#post470346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not scientific, that's something only deific power can accomplish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing is scientific except the scientific method. Everything else is either described under a scientific theory (subject to re-evaluation at any time of new evidence contradicts previous findings or if a new model explains it better), or is a curiosity to be further studied in hopes of developing a theory to explain it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-06-2015, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T15:12:29-07:00","id":470406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Take for example, the traditional wizard who casts spells with verbal incantations and gestures. How can that ever be science? You're basically saying the wizard is asking the universe (usually in Latin) if it will stop abiding the rules for a moment, and the universe says &quot;Sure!&quot; </div> </div> </div>Well, it doesn't work, and it doesn't really make sense either. It works in fiction because it's a trope people recognise and therefore don't bother to question. Why does Harry Potter speak cod-Latin to do magic? Don't know, don't care, it's not relevant to the plot. That trope actually has origins in real 'magic' but in that case there's an actual body of quasi-scientific theory as to what's going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T17:23:42-07:00","id":470499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=470173#post470173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Machine isn't a computer, it's a system, a system of oppression, a system of control, a system of maintenance of the status quo. Farmers building the pyramids in their off-season are a part of the system, putting together infrastructure in specific locations to disrupt or alter the flow of energy into and out of Shadow/Hedge/Twilight/Supernal. Kids in school doing pointless homework are unknowingly crunching numbers for it. Stonehenge is all that remains of an ancient infrastructure, but it's memetically important in humanity so it had the place declared a monument and set up armed guards. It built the pyramid in China to house a tiny scale model of the Empire complete with rivers of flowing mercury so that it had a back-up in case the real thing broke down. It's in stars, symbology, the paths of ancient trade routes. The cogs and gears are just the parts making noise.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;God created everything by number, weight, and measure.&quot;<br /> <br /> Incidentally, Sir Isaac Newton had a lot to say about God, as could be expected from a physicist and a theologian <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Religious_views_of_Isaac_Newton#The_Bible\" target=\"_blank\">heavily into Bible prophecy</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>This Being governs all things, not as the soul of the world, but as Lord over all</b>: And on account of his dominion he is wont to be called Lord God <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christ_Pantocrator#Meaning\" target=\"_blank\">\u03c0\u03b1\u03bd\u03c4\u03bf\u03ba\u03c1\u00e1\u03c4\u03c9\u03c1</a> or Universal Ruler. For <i>God</i> is a relative word, and has a respect to servants; <b>and <i>Deity</i> is the dominion of God, not over his own body, as those imagine who fancy God to be the soul of the world, but over servants.</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T21:50:39-07:00","id":470903,"title":"","content":"I know you already said you get it, but I was really disappointed by that because it meant I couldn't use this image.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=470346#post470346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get what you're saying that science is constantly changed based on what we observe, but again, I still think that's pretty arrogant or doesn't hold up in some conditions. Take for example, the traditional wizard who casts spells with verbal incantations and gestures. How can that ever be science? You're basically saying the wizard is asking the universe (usually in Latin) if it will stop abiding the rules for a moment, and the universe says &quot;Sure!&quot;<br /> <br /> And then, of course, there's the component of magic being fueled by willpower. The mage / wizard / sorcerer or whatever is disobeying science because they want to. Science isn't about getting what you want simply because you want it. I want the family pick up truck to turn into a laborghini when I honk the horn 5 times... doesn't mean the universe will grant my wish.<br /> <br /> That's not scientific, that's something only deific power can accomplish.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://imgs.xkcd.com/comics/the_difference.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> From: <a href=\"https://xkcd.com/242/\" target=\"_blank\">https://xkcd.com/242/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T01:50:24-07:00","id":480011,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised that no one has pointed out that in mage there are technognostics who believe that there is literally nothing magic can do that science can't potentially do as well, it just hasn't been figured out yet. <br /> <br /> Except the God-Machine did figure it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T04:01:34-07:00","id":480052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=480011#post480011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm surprised that no one has pointed out that in mage there are technognostics who believe that there is literally nothing magic can do that science can't potentially do as well, it just hasn't been figured out yet.<br /> <br /> Except the God-Machine did figure it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or a Mage figured out how to make a machine that could. There's really no way of telling given the time-shenanegins that both could pull.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T12:22:39-07:00","id":480591,"title":"","content":"That would involve assuming mages had something to do with the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> Fuuuuck that noise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T12:37:52-07:00","id":480600,"title":"","content":"An archmage somewhere at some point: &quot;Whoops.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T13:21:31-07:00","id":480645,"title":"","content":"I'm with Arc on this one. And generally against making Mages the center of the universe ('the center of the universe' in this case meaning 'had something to do with everything'). They're not Forrest Gump.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T13:28:52-07:00","id":480649,"title":"","content":"<b>Ex</b>iled <b>Arch</b>-angels. That is all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T13:51:29-07:00","id":480681,"title":"","content":"The only G-M explanation in Mage I liked was the rumor that it is an elaborate Mystery Play for the re-ascension of a fallen god. <br /> My own personal explanation is that it's Autocthonia - the only survivor of the cWoD and possibly Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T14:17:59-07:00","id":480703,"title":"","content":"&quot;What the hell is Null Space and why does it need a Viator?&quot; - Potential last words of pretty much any nwod denizen you'd care to name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T14:26:34-07:00","id":480709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=480645#post480645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm with Arc on this one. And generally against making Mages the center of the universe ('the center of the universe' in this case meaning 'had something to do with everything'). They're not Forrest Gump.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, although the God Machine is almost a worse offender, given that it's presented as though it's secretly behind everything in what's currently the de-facto 2e core rule book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T15:13:39-07:00","id":480758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=480709#post480709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, although the God Machine is almost a worse offender, given that it's presented as though it's secretly behind everything in what's currently the de-facto 2e core rule book.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that book, which is explicitly centered around it, and in DtD, which is <i>also</i> explicitly centered around it and its creations. It gets basically no mention in VtR2 or WtF2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T15:22:12-07:00","id":480804,"title":"","content":"And I'd even disagree with the interpretation that the God-Machine is behind &quot;everything&quot; even in the God-Machine Chronicle. I distinctly remember multiple supernatural occurrences, most notably ghosts in several God-Machine stories, whose existence has no cosmological link to the Machine. They are used by it, but they are not <i>of</i> it. Then there are spirits, another branch of clearly distinct supernatural. The closest the GMC comes to presenting the God-Machine as being behind everything is by having all of the sample stories in the God-Machine Chronicle involve the God-Machine in some manner. Weird, that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T16:11:53-07:00","id":480839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=480758#post480758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that book, which is explicitly centered around it, and in DtD, which is <i>also</i> explicitly centered around it and its creations. It gets basically no mention in VtR2 or WtF2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and Mage isn't mentioned in those books either. It doesn't stop some people from trying to tie Mage into everything and it doesn't stop other people from trying to tie the God-Machine into everything either. What I'm saying is, the GM gets nearly as much &quot;center of the universe&quot; treatment from fans as Mage does, in just the short time it's been around. I hypothesize that this is due to its prominent position in a core-esque blue book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T16:19:12-07:00","id":480847,"title":"","content":"Yeah but people were doing that even when it was a lil' fiction piece in the 1E Corebook. The idea is just something people liked and decided to latch onto. The GMC pretty much exists <i>because</i> people were so into the idea of the GM and were eating up any little links writers would throw into other books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T16:36:40-07:00","id":480877,"title":"","content":"Psst!<br /> <br /> Kereboi are behind everything. The GM is the Kerebos of the world. Because it is an underworld realm. You heard it here first. <i>You are already dead.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T16:41:41-07:00","id":480905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=480877#post480877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Psst!<br /> <br /> Kereboi are behind everything. The GM is the Kerebos of the world. Because it is an underworld realm. You heard it here first. <i>You are already dead.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I think I see what you did there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T18:01:38-07:00","id":480958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=480839#post480839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, and Mage isn't mentioned in those books either. It doesn't stop some people from trying to tie Mage into everything and it doesn't stop other people from trying to tie the God-Machine into everything either. What I'm saying is, the GM gets nearly as much &quot;center of the universe&quot; treatment from fans as Mage does, in just the short time it's been around. I hypothesize that this is due to its prominent position in a core-esque blue book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always got the impression that it was an emerging power. One growing in strength due to the modern age.<br /> I also got the impression that is was a god not THE GOD. Just one of many possible Powers and Principalities in the world of Darkness.<br /> After all if you found Ktulu was real and a godlike being you would hope there were opposing forces out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T18:09:16-07:00","id":480961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=480958#post480958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always got the impression that it was an emerging power. One growing in strength due to the modern age.<br /> I also got the impression that is was a god not THE GOD. Just one of many possible Powers and Principalities in the world of Darkness.<br /> After all if you found Ktulu was real and a godlike being you would hope there were opposing forces out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that's a cool interpretation.<br /> <br /> In case it's still not clear, I am <b>not</b> saying I personally think the God Machine is behind everything. I'm saying I have seen just as much of people trying to tie the God Machine into everything as I have seen people doing the same with Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T19:42:57-07:00","id":481039,"title":"","content":"I rarely see people tie stuff into Mage. In fact I usually see people point out over and over that a Mage centric name for certain little understood areas literally is used as a make word for &quot;Shit we don't understand.&quot; I see people work to create a game cosmology for a real or hypothetical game that is going to involve the God Machine and other setting's metaphysical elements, which makes perfect sense when you're looking to tell those sort of games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 04-14-2015, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T20:36:53-07:00","id":481073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=480961#post480961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In case it's still not clear, I am <b>not</b> saying I personally think the God Machine is behind everything. I'm saying I have seen just as much of people trying to tie the God Machine into everything as I have seen people doing the same with Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in case those people ever <i>actually show up</i>, they will get just as much of my scorn as the multifarious Chicken Littles that are presently making nuisances of themselves warning against the specter of Mage Supremacy or Deus Est Machina Uber Alles.<br /> <br /> I'm sure they'll be here any week now, but in the meantime, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=303848#post303848\">as I've said before</a>, <b>could we <i>not, </i>please?</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T21:25:17-07:00","id":481106,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty confused by this debate/discussion. It says in the title of the very book it's a God Machine &quot;Chronicle.&quot; It's just an idea to base chronicles on. Use it or don't, why slag those who like it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","name":"n_a_anyon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T22:12:44-07:00","id":481120,"title":"","content":"Mages have a habit of sticking their noses into everything. That's not the same as being behind everything, or even <i>claiming to be</i> behind everything. I have no problem with how they're being handled right now. <br /> <br /> OTOH, I don't want the God-Machine to be featured in the second edition core book; and once it's out, I'd like <b>God-Machine Chronicle</b> to be rebranded as a <b>Demon</b> supplement. I don't want anything that would give the impression that the God-Machine is in any way central to the World of Darkness. Really, I don't think that any one antagonist should be featured in the core book; I'd rather see a selection of monsters that don't fit neatly into any of the boxes that the existing gamelines have established \u2014 essentially a blue-book version of the <b>Night Horrors</b> concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T23:07:33-07:00","id":481150,"title":"","content":"God-Machine Chronicles isn't a Demon supplement, it's a bluebook supplement.<br /> <br /> The Book of Spirits is not a Werewolf supplement, it's a bluebook supplement.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T23:25:51-07:00","id":481157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481073#post481073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in case those people ever <i>actually show up</i>, they will get just as much of my scorn as the multifarious Chicken Littles that are presently making nuisances of themselves warning against the specter of Mage Supremacy or Deus Est Machina Uber Alles.<br /> <br /> I'm sure they'll be here any week now, but in the meantime, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=303848#post303848\">as I've said before</a>, <b>could we <i>not, </i>please?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>It's not like this is without precedence. How many Changeling threads did we get trying to tie into the God-Machine's physics recently? At least two?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T23:28:16-07:00","id":481159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481150#post481150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God-Machine Chronicles isn't a Demon supplement, it's a bluebook supplement.<br /> <br /> The Book of Spirits is not a Werewolf supplement, it's a bluebook supplement.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This. So Much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T00:06:21-07:00","id":481191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481157#post481157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not like this is without precedence. How many Changeling threads did we get trying to tie into the God-Machine's physics recently? At least two?</div> </div> </div> </div>The earlier of which was unanimously decried and the later of which still saw little in the way of support after it made only the vaguest attempts to tie itself into Lost lore.<br /> <br /> You'll recall the histrionics that occurred when <i>Imperial Mysteries </i>came out, I hope, and that much more of them came from other people popping into the Mage boards than the other way around.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the crossover kids have not, to my knowledge, belittled a freelancer's attempt to engage with a get-creative thread in a fashion that was not to their liking.<br /> <br /> There's a world of difference between getting overenthusiastic and monomaniacal about the applications of nWoD toolbox theory and <i>insulting the thing you don't like and the people who don't share your opinion about it.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-15-2015, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T00:08:31-07:00","id":481192,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>A friendly reminder not directed at any given poster to stay chillaxed in the thread. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T00:24:47-07:00","id":481193,"title":"","content":"Hey, I love the God Machine. Mage isn't my favorite thing, but I've got no beef with it. I'm also cool with people fiddling around with crossover however they like. Just saying, in the case of both Mage and the God-Machine, I've both seen and proposed more than a few theories that make one or the other very central to the setting. Less so for other lines, except maybe Changeling. These kinds of theories can be highly appropriate to some games, or highly inappropriate to others. It's all good, do what works for your games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T01:28:40-07:00","id":481223,"title":"","content":"Really, my original point was more that the machine doesn't necessarily have to have been the thing to have figured things out - the creator could be an entirely different beast than the Machine who created it to tap into parts of reality they had no access to. I used Mage as an example because out-of-control experiments are a big part of their schtick. Though an argument could also be made for Promethean - I'm just currently involved in a Mage-centric game so I'm used to thinking on a power level where the rules could easily support accidentally creating an occult engine that grew into a god.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481120#post481120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OTOH, I don't want the God-Machine to be featured in the second edition core book; and once it's out, I'd like <b>God-Machine Chronicle</b> to be rebranded as a <b>Demon</b> supplement. I don't want anything that would give the impression that the God-Machine is in any way central to the World of Darkness. Really, I don't think that any one antagonist should be featured in the core book; I'd rather see a selection of monsters that don't fit neatly into any of the boxes that the existing gamelines have established \u2014 essentially a blue-book version of the <b>Night Horrors</b> concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>So much this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T02:01:13-07:00","id":481231,"title":"","content":"As a Mage fan, I think from now on, whenever I encounter this kind of discussion, I'm gonna post this.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaveBrookshaw;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages don't try to fit everything they experience into their cosmology. Mages, even in 1st edition, <i>get more powerful</i> when they encounter something genuinely new to them. They are not the powered-by-sophistry paradigm mages of Mage: The Ascension, who have to explain everything according to their own rules. Mage: The Awakening mages <i>love</i> it when they can't explain something by their own rules, and their internal mythology is based on the idea that <i>nothing</i> apart from their own spells is the result of the Supernal, because of the Abyss. They anger and upset other supernatural beings in the World of Darkness by being perpetually curious and poking themselves into other monsters' business.<br /> <br /> Some mage fans did not get the memo. Many more fans of other gamelines didn't either.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T03:17:31-07:00","id":481241,"title":"","content":"@BlueBiscuit<br /> That's kinda a different issue, though they're often conflated. That's about in-character knowledge, whilst this is more about the actual cosmology of the setting. Even if you make the G-M the personal servant of the Exarchs, most magi aren't going to be any the wiser.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T07:45:23-07:00","id":481302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481150#post481150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God-Machine Chronicles isn't a Demon supplement, it's a bluebook supplement.<br /> <br /> The Book of Spirits is not a Werewolf supplement, it's a bluebook supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh! Can I try? <br /> <br /> The Book of the Dead is not a Geist supplement, it's a bluebook supplement. <br /> <br /> Slashers is not a Hunter supplement, it's a bluebook supplement. <br /> <br /> Skinchangers is not a Werewolf supplement, it's a bluebook supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T08:30:38-07:00","id":481323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481302#post481302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh! Can I try?<br /> <br /> The Book of the Dead is not a Geist supplement, it's a bluebook supplement.<br /> <br /> Slashers is not a Hunter supplement, it's a bluebook supplement.<br /> <br /> Skinchangers is not a Werewolf supplement, it's a bluebook supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I am not positive about <i>Book of the Dead </i>or <i>Slashers</i>, <i><b>Skinchangers </b></i>is indeed a Blue Book Supplement. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T08:49:17-07:00","id":481330,"title":"","content":"Slashers has Hunter's distinctive section title format at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T09:01:26-07:00","id":481332,"title":"","content":"Book of the Dead is bluebook, Slashers really seems to straddle the fence. It looks like it was originally designed to be Hunter, as the book is set up like other hunter books, the introduction goes on and on about hunters, 'But this book is about the hunters, too. How do hunters handle a slasher? Have the hunters formed any compacts or conspiracies specifically bent on dealing with slashers (answer: yup). What tools do hunter characters have to help put slashers down into the ground for good\u2026 and what tools do the slashers have to fight back?'<br /> <br /> I can't recall but I think the skull on the edge is a mortal, non-flaming ones, and it says World of Darkness on the cover, rather than Hunter the Vigil. If I had to guess I'd say it was designed for Hunter and changed at the last minute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T09:04:29-07:00","id":481353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481302#post481302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh! Can I try?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can make your counterargument without engaging in such an obnoxious break in character. Reasons to be disgusted with people are not an appreciated gift.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Book of the Dead is not a Geist supplement, it's a bluebook supplement. </div> </div> </div>Chapter full of Bound widgets aside, it presents a distinctly different take on the Underworld to what <i>Geist</i> does. <i>The Book of Spirits</i> does not have a comparable <i>Werewolf</i> section and shares BotD's &quot;the realm in mortal consciousness&quot; style of first chapter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Slashers is not a Hunter supplement, it's a bluebook supplement. </div> </div> </div>You're sending some mixed messages here with this terrible basic-sarcasm thing you're doing, seeing as this is explicitly false by virtue of the &quot;Next Book&quot; blurb in <i>Witch Finders</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Skinchangers is not a Werewolf supplement, it's a bluebook supplement. </div> </div> </div>As has been highlighted, this one's just a statement of fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-15-2015, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T09:09:17-07:00","id":481355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481302#post481302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh! Can I try?<br /> <br /> The Book of the Dead is not a Geist supplement, it's a bluebook supplement.<br /> <br /> Slashers is not a Hunter supplement, it's a bluebook supplement.<br /> <br /> Skinchangers is not a Werewolf supplement, it's a bluebook supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All these are true? They deal with subject matter pertinent to some gamelines, but are useful for more than just Geist, Hunter, and Werewolf. The Underworld and ghosts are something that exist in every gameline. Slasher's can be used for more than just hunters (though,I don't see Hunter as too distinct from bluebook, except on the focus on how one interacts with the supernatural) and Skinchangers is about shapeshifters, but they are not tied to the legacy of Father/Mother Wolf and Luna. <br /> <br /> They could potentially be included in any game line. Just as the God-Machine can. It's never FORCED for you to accept it, but it's an option and some people are going to take it, even if you arn't. So what if a Changeling ST wants to tie their game to the G-M? That's their choice, and not anyone elses. Hell, they may even come to these boards wishing to discuss their idea, because talking and fleshing out ideas is fun. I don't see anything wrong with it. None of it has any effect on the corebooks, it's all a toolbox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T09:14:44-07:00","id":481360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481353#post481353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're sending some mixed messages here with this terrible basic-sarcasm thing you're doing, seeing as this is explicitly false by virtue of the &quot;Next Book&quot; blurb in <i>Witch Finders</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, if I remember correctly, Slasher was meant to be an Hunter book (hence being published in Witch Finder) but then was changed into a Blue Book when it was officially released. This is presented by the title &quot;World of Darkness- Slasher&quot;, as being something of the general WoD line, instead of &quot;Hunter the Vigil&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T09:18:40-07:00","id":481361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481360#post481360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, if I remember correctly, Slasher was meant to be an Hunter book (hence being published in Witch Finder) but then was changed into a Blue Book when it was officially released. This is presented by the title &quot;World of Darkness- Slasher&quot;, as being something of the general WoD line, instead of &quot;Hunter the Vigil&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is that <i>Slasher</i> is blatantly and observably in a different boat than the others and that calling it a Hunter supplement is <i>especially</i> different from calling the GMC a &quot;supplement&quot; for a gameline that <i>didn't come out until over half a year after the rules update did.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-15-2015, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T09:28:38-07:00","id":481369,"title":"","content":"Hey, I'm not supporting making the GMC into a Demon supplement. The devs and writers themselves said that the GMC is a blue book because no current element in the WoD was tied to all of the different gamelines as it was. Before Demon, making the God Machine into a Chronicle book was a logical choice. The fact that Demon use the God Machine as a central piece of cosmology doesn't change it. All I did was to point out that Slasher is also a Blue Book, as it was decided by the devs and writers, and correcting a false piece of information. That's all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T09:34:45-07:00","id":481372,"title":"","content":"Finally found it, yes it has a blood-splattered mortal skull. On a slightly greenish blue cover. The interior is unabashedly Hunter, but the exterior hints at the blue books. As Satchel pointed out the interior mentions Spirit Slayers, 'Coming Up Next For Hunter: the Vigil' while blue books traditionally say something to the extent of, 'For Use With The World of Darkness Rulebook,' with an image of first edition core.<br /> <br /> Anyways, 'removing' the God Machine is just a matter of not including it in everything but Demon the Descent. It's not a core part of the rules, the cult system isn't tied to it, the ephemeral rules work similarly for spirits and ghosts as well as angels. Even its references in other books are so small as can easily be overlooked or be the 'something else' that always exists in World of Darkness. Apparently Dave Brookshaw is 'aggressively' removing references to it in Mage the Awakening second edition so once they publish World of Darkness Second Edition core rules there will probably be a lot less of the misinformed complaining about the God Machine being a metaplot or being 'forced' into every game or whatever complaints others have heard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-15-2015, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T11:40:10-07:00","id":481433,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd be willing to get rid of the God-Machine. Not because of what it is but because of how it is. I often hear things about how the GM is so big it can't interact with you because that would be like a human trying to interact with a single molecule. But then right after that I hear that the GM can rewire your brain and create a whole new life for you.<br /> <br /> How am I supposed to feel I have a chance against this? WoD is not Call of Cthulhu. The fun does not lie in how long I can stay alive. NWoD went above and beyond in order to break from OWoD's habbit that every threat is cosmic-scaled, and then they give us the God-Machine, a giant robot that spans the whole universe and lives in all realities at once. As far as I'm concerned, it will never make an appearance in any of my games (and I'll never play Demon, because it's the canonical nemesis to every character). Also, <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481372#post481372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Apparently Dave Brookshaw is 'aggressively' removing references to it in Mage the Awakening second edition</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more than happy to read this. I loved the Machine in Promethean, because it was implicit that it was manipulating everything, and we had nothing to confirm that it was an omnipotent-omniscient being. Since GMC-RU the only explanation I hear from all players is &quot;The God-Machine created this for...&quot;. I refuse to believe that Idigams, Vampires, Prometheans and all the supernal realms are a creation from the God-Machine, but when it's written in the core book, it's pushing me away from the game. For the same reason Mage was pushing me away from it: answering every question with a single answer is, in my opinion, a bad way of answering questions.<br /> <br /> TL;DR -\u00ad thanks Dave","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T11:55:14-07:00","id":481442,"title":"","content":"No offense MO, but I get the feeling you haven't thoroughly read the God-Machine Chronicle. The God-Machine is quite explicitly not omniscient nor omnipotent. Its influence is limited only to the physical world, and it relies on complex infrastructure, which takes a great deal of time and preparation, in order to complete occult matrices. It is a powerful, but strictly temporal and limited enemy, and stories about it are meant to focus on the protagonists gaining small victories against it, by exploiting linchpins (weak points in its infrastructure) to destroy occult matricies or prevent them from being completed. There's even a sample story in which the protagonists prevent the end of the world. As for Demon, the GM is definitely not the canonical nemesis of every PC. It's more of a menacing piece of background material that forms the impetus for the espionage aspects. Yeah, you don't want to be found by the GM or its angels, but as long as you take proper precautions, that doesn't even have to be the focal point of the game.<br /> <br /> Now, if you don't like the God-Machine, that's fine, nobody can fault you for that. But most of your criticisms of it are just factually inaccurate, so it might be worth giving a second look, since the reasons you give for disliking it are actually not the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T12:02:31-07:00","id":481448,"title":"","content":"Actually, I enjoyed having a reference here and there about the God Machine, and while I pretty liked the GMC it feels like that it killed all of those delicate implications for all future generations about players who see the GM and scream- &quot;it's a metaplot!&quot;, which is kinda annoying. The GM is not a metaplot, it never was and I never got the feeling that those implications were meant to hint that it controls/created everything (maybe because I'm a fervent believer that every splat was created independently from the other, and that the GM is simply one of many &quot;God Machine level beings&quot; who exist in the world). I do understand that what Dave is doing is truly for the best of Mage and that it is the right call considering the reaction of certain fans- but I can't but feel disappointed for not feeling the rush again from finding a new God Machine Easter Egg.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T12:10:54-07:00","id":481451,"title":"","content":"We're beginning to talk in directions now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T12:15:53-07:00","id":481453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481433#post481433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How am I supposed to feel I have a chance against this? WoD is not Call of Cthulhu. The fun does not lie in how long I can stay alive. NWoD went above and beyond in order to break from OWoD's habbit that every threat is cosmic-scaled, and then they give us the God-Machine, a giant robot that spans the whole universe and lives in all realities at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I'm very sympathetic to feelings like this \u2014 I've never had much of any interest in Call of Cthulhu for pretty much mostly this reason. But one of the big strengths I loved about The God-Machine Chronicle as a book (not the rules update, the full book) was how it's all presented in a format that is very practical about the ground's-eye view of things. The upshot is that the bigness of the God-Machine is its weakness as much as its strength. Its parts are poorly aligned and prone to miscommunication; the right hand doesn't know what the left is doing.<br /> <br /> It's not monolithic, and so &quot;the God-Machine&quot; can't rewire your brain or do much of anything, really, not in the sense that any agent of the God-Machine has the means to do this. It has lots and lots of projects all around the place, each of which can do some scary thing, but they don't share resources well; one station might want to rewire your brain but have to kidnap you and ship you on an interstate convoy to reach the nearest brain-rewiring station, affording you or your friends plenty of time to bust you out.<br /> <br /> And that's also where you've got your chance: since &quot;the God-Machine&quot; isn't really one thing so much as lots of loosely connected projects, and your chances against a given project at a time are vastly better than your chances taking on every project in the world at once. Destroying every project in the world is a feat on par with destroying the Exarchs or exterminating the Moon-Banished, but destroying the God-Machine's influence over upstate New York is entirely doable, even for a group of mortal humans (for whom the GMC is designed).<br /> <br /> The book does a pretty good job of setting down limits for the thing as a whole, too. Its projects mostly span the material realm; it doesn't penetrate very far into the otherworlds by default. There are several story hooks in the book about the God-Machine miscalcualting or getting interfered with and the consequences running amok; it's hardly all-controlling. And every project is designed to have some kind of Achilles heel that presents a practical means of tackling the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T12:24:17-07:00","id":481483,"title":"","content":"No offense to you personally Magnum Opus, but that's exactly the type of negative post I think these boards could do without. You'd be &quot;willing to get rid of&quot; the God Machine? Who's forcing you to keep it in the first place? What is the point of that post besides espousing your distaste for the God Machine idea for several paragraphs? Frankly I'd rather ignore your post, but given the recent discussion about negativity in the Monday Meeting, I thought I'd bring it up. &quot;When it's written in the core book, it's pushing me away from the game.&quot; As Charlaquin said, you seem to have confused the enthusiasm of people who are fans of certain ideas about the God Machine for genuine canon. To go so far as to let that push you away from the game, and to come here and make a lengthy post saying so, just seems unnecessarily negative to me. You're letting your own hyperbole get to your head.<br /> <br /> Obviously the God Machine is not just a chronicle idea in Demon, but as the Promethean developer said regarding humanity and the Pilgrimage, all games require some buy-in, and if you don't like that buy-in then the game isn't for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","name":"n_a_anyon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T13:03:49-07:00","id":481534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481448#post481448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I enjoyed having a reference here and there about the God Machine, and while I pretty liked the GMC it feels like that it killed all of those delicate implications for all future generations about players who see the GM and scream- &quot;it's a metaplot!&quot;, which is kinda annoying. The GM is not a metaplot, it never was and I never got the feeling that those implications were meant to hint that it controls/created everything (maybe because I'm a fervent believer that every splat was created independently from the other, and that the GM is simply one of many &quot;God Machine level beings&quot; who exist in the world). I do understand that what Dave is doing is truly for the best of Mage and that it is the right call considering the reaction of certain fans- but I can't but feel disappointed for not feeling the rush again from finding a new God Machine Easter Egg.</div> </div> </div> </div>People have been misusing the term &quot;metaplot&quot; for a long time now, and I would not be surprised since the inception of the NWoD. My guess is Magnum probably just confused a combination of hearsay, actual written elements,etc. Most of us have done that a time or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T14:48:17-07:00","id":481604,"title":"","content":"First, I'd like to apologize for any negativity that might have been taken from my post. Second, I feel no offense coming from people criticising my post and I think we're doing a great job at keeping this respectful.<br /> <br /> I love WoD. Let that be clear. I've been playing for a long time now, long before the God-Machine was given it's rightful place. Thank you Charlaquin for pointing flaws in my knowledge, I guess I'll have to have a second look at it. Again, I know no one's forcing me to use it in my game - I've explicitly stated that it never appeared in one and, as of now, will not be making an appearance. But since it's a huge part of the buy-in, I feel like I'm missing on something. Is it the new overarching plot for WoD? No. I don't think so. Am I the only one to have problems with the current way the God-Machine is portrayed? I don't think so either.<br /> <br /> When I said &quot;Getting rid of&quot; the God-Machine, I meant in the rules, not in the whole game and not for all eternity. I actually used the God-Machine in a post-apocalyptic LARP I was at, so it's not the Idea that I dislike. I just want a dissociation from rules and the GM, and if possible as few mentions of the GM in other game lines as possible because, as stated by LostLight, I enjoy my splats being distinct rather than fused in a single perfectly aligned universe with clear hierarchies.<br /> <br /> As far as fighting projects go, I, as a player, do not feel rewarded for defeating a building or a train (as demon-possessed as can be) as much as an agent. Especially if the organization I defeat is only a drop in an ocean, because I understand that the real menace is still looming over and waiting for me to turn my back to reimplement its project. I feel like I did nothing except for the few weeks to come. Especially if my enemy is a pure-logic machine of cosmic-scale powers. I have friends, lovers, family, weaknesses. It has logic and objectives. I was in a single game during which we had to fight the God-Machine, and it felt nothing like fair or fun - we were powerless.<br /> <br /> Honestly I might not be seeing the GM as others are, but then again if I have to read 2 full books cover-to-cover in order to understand why it's supposed to be fun, I think something's wrong in the presentation. <br /> <br /> As a last note I'd like to ask you: what single story should I read in order to enjoy &amp; understand the most of what the GM is supposed to be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T15:18:57-07:00","id":481659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481604#post481604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a last note I'd like to ask you: what single story should I read in order to enjoy &amp; understand the most of what the GM is supposed to be?</div> </div> </div> </div>The god-machine can inspire a lot of different kinds of plots, so it's hard to choose just one story. <br /> <br /> The one that really gets me is the series of work emails at the beginning of the God-Machine chronicle, but it's probably not the best example of how the G-M is usually presented. <br /> Thnetosis from Demon's Interface anthology was pretty great, as was Unicorn Crossing from the same volume. <br /> <br /> If you don't like defeating an impersonal machine, that's fine! The impersonal stuff is there to give it some institutional weight - kind of like opposing a faceless corporation.<br /> <br /> It's true that the God-Machine as a whole thinks on too big of a scale to interact with individual humans, but that's why it forges Angels. Angels are supposed to be logical, implacable instruments of His Mechanical Will, but that's not usually how it shakes out. They frequently settle into their roles just a little too well and I think that's what makes them relatable. <br /> <br /> One Angel is designed to tempt demons back to the Fold, but she gets used to the material pleasures - cars, pizza, someone on the couch next to her; and she teeters close to falling without making the plunge. I think Angels are just human enough to make the God-Machine relatable. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T15:59:30-07:00","id":481696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481604#post481604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I said &quot;Getting rid of&quot; the God-Machine, I meant in the rules, not in the whole game and not for all eternity. I actually used the God-Machine in a post-apocalyptic LARP I was at, so it's not the Idea that I dislike. I just want a dissociation from rules and the GM, and if possible as few mentions of the GM in other game lines as possible because, as stated by LostLight, I enjoy my splats being distinct rather than fused in a single perfectly aligned universe with clear hierarchies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do you see it integrated in the rules? Or if you just mean branding the first and central splash of the second edition nWoD rules as &quot;The God-Machine Rules Update,&quot; and leaving some fiction from the God-Machine Chronicle interspersed across it, was a misstep, I'm comfortable agreeing with that sentiment. (Even being a fan of the GMC, I find the fiction letters interspersed across the rules appendix really inconvenient and annoying, that's bad layout.) My hope is that, to try to avoid triggering this sentiment, the upcoming full nWoD 2e core rulebook will more clearly cordon off the God-Machine antagonist material as optional, more in line with what Requiem did with the strix and Forsaken the idigam \u2014 those are books that put their easy-use antagonists right up front but still make clear that there's a lot to being a vampire or werewolf besides fighting Your Archnemeses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481604#post481604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as fighting projects go, I, as a player, do not feel rewarded for defeating a building or a train (as demon-possessed as can be) as much as an agent. Especially if the organization I defeat is only a drop in an ocean, because I understand that the real menace is still looming over and waiting for me to turn my back to reimplement its project. I feel like I did nothing except for the few weeks to come. Especially if my enemy is a pure-logic machine of cosmic-scale powers. I have friends, lovers, family, weaknesses. It has logic and objectives. I was in a single game during which we had to fight the God-Machine, and it felt nothing like fair or fun - we were powerless.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds to me like it's as much your Storyteller's approach to the God-Machine as the written material that left a sour taste in your mouth. Which, well, the material isn't innocent in allowing those impressions to be made, but you're not generally meant to feel like every project you defeat is a meaningless drop in the ocean, or that the Machine is constantly looming over you.<br /> <br /> The Machine isn't meant to be presented as an agent. It's an organization of agents, essentially; the kind that's larger than having one leader to pinpoint, like how the CIA isn't just an extension of whoever is the Director of Central Intelligence. The Machine is not the antagonist for a story; the Screaming Angel is, or the chief economic officer of Eidolon Marketing, or the viral control program living in the city's electrical grid. It's important that the projects aren't just presented as all faceless extensions of the larger Machine; they're staffed by middle managers and angels that have their own personalities and goals and outlooks (yes, even angels disagree on logistics \u2014 the God Machine can often end up fighting <i>itself).</i><br /> <br /> The God-Machine book, again, has some good material specifically addressing the issue that you don't want your players coming away feeling demoralized in a futile struggle that will only end when they slip up and die. Projects can't just be replaced; they're based on confluences that don't repeat for hundreds or thousands of years, or cost tons of manpower to reproduce. Each project defeated by an outside force is a major setback, and yes, for that outside force, a lasting victory.<br /> <br /> That's the spirit it's meant in. I think the GMC book does a good job conveying it \u2014 you don't really need to read two full books cover to cover, the Introduction does a pretty good job right there in my opinion. But I can acknowledge that the information is parceled out such that if you're paying peripheral attention since you're already focused on other stories, you can end up with just a little summary that conveys something different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481604#post481604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a last note I'd like to ask you: what single story should I read in order to enjoy &amp; understand the most of what the GM is supposed to be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most important and most effective read in terms of understanding the God-Machine? The Introduction of the God-Machine Chronicle book. It's dense, efficient, and does a good job of showing you what the parts are, what they look like, and why.<br /> <br /> Most important and most effective game fiction example representative of what an adventure against the God-Machine looks like? Stew Wilson's Go Back, from the God-Machine Chronicle Anthology short story collection. Most notably, while most of the stories in that book are horror stories more appropriate for setting the stage for some PCs to come in and address the situation, Go Back is about a character who ends up ahead in the conflict, and ends the story positioned to begin to push back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 04-15-2015, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T16:33:23-07:00","id":481712,"title":"","content":"We're all awesome and I love all of you ^.^<br /> <br /> &quot;The one that really gets me is the series of work emails at the beginning of the God-Machine chronicle.&quot;<br /> That fiction legitimately gave me the creeps when I read it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","name":"n_a_anyon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T17:08:26-07:00","id":481731,"title":"","content":"I think the Godmachine is an interesting and compelling antagonist, personally... but why does it need to be referenced at all in the upcoming 2e bluebook? It already *has* its own book. The Godmachine Chronicles. Even putting in an optional section about Godmachine antagonists feels like unneeded space, particularly again because one of the originally compelling things to me about NWoD was its explicitly toolbox approach to horror that encouraged everything from urban-cryptids to modern Conanesque sorcerers lurking in the shadows, with no even implied underlying cosmology except that ghosts and spirits were a thing... entities that already had copious background lore in the real world and didn't need their own interpretation to include.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say that Book of the Dead and Book of Spirits aren't two of my favorite books in all of NWoD - they are... but just as I feel an in-depth explanation, or even meaningful reference to the NWoD Underworld would have been out of place in the Blue Book, so too do I feel like reference to the Machine in the Blue Book 2.0 would be out of place and at cross-purposes to the toolbox nature of the old Blue Book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>n_a_anyon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481483#post481483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No offense to you personally Magnum Opus, but that's exactly the type of negative post I think these boards could do without. You'd be &quot;willing to get rid of&quot; the God Machine? Who's forcing you to keep it in the first place? What is the point of that post besides espousing your distaste for the God Machine idea for several paragraphs? Frankly I'd rather ignore your post, but given the recent discussion about negativity in the Monday Meeting, I thought I'd bring it up. &quot;When it's written in the core book, it's pushing me away from the game.&quot; As Charlaquin said, you seem to have confused the enthusiasm of people who are fans of certain ideas about the God Machine for genuine canon. To go so far as to let that push you away from the game, and to come here and make a lengthy post saying so, just seems unnecessarily negative to me. You're letting your own hyperbole get to your head.</div> </div> </div> </div>...except that this is a product being sold to people for money, it isn't a fan splat. If everyone who felt alienated by the direction of the game stayed silent you would risk a silent exodus of paying customers for reasons the devs were never aware of. I would go so far as saying that negativity directed at the product, rather than the producers, is a vitally important part of any creative process. Indeed, I think the worst thing that can happen to a community is for it to become a self-serving echo-chamber of undiluted supportiveness which silences dissenting opinions under the guise of stepford-wives styles of politeness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T18:10:17-07:00","id":481795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481731#post481731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, I think the worst thing that can happen to a community is for it to become a self-serving echo-chamber of undiluted supportiveness which silences dissenting opinions under the guise of stepford-wives styles of politeness.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've also literally compared your own disagreement with set elements of the core mechanics to disagreeing with <i>fascism</i>, so I feel as though there's a very large middle ground being excluded here in the name of hyperbole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T19:05:52-07:00","id":481821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481731#post481731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If everyone who felt alienated by the direction of the game stayed silent you would risk a silent exodus of paying customers for reasons the devs were never aware of. I would go so far as saying that negativity directed at the product, rather than the producers, is a vitally important part of any creative process. Indeed, I think the worst thing that can happen to a community is for it to become a self-serving echo-chamber of undiluted supportiveness which silences dissenting opinions under the guise of stepford-wives styles of politeness.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one's silencing you or other dissenting opinions. To the contrary, quite a few of us who enjoy the God-Machine have also enjoyed chatting about how to run a Demon game with none of the God-Machine's techgnosticism. Heck, there are at least two upcoming official supplements I can think of that are running with this idea.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path has 11ish nWoD gamelines, 10 cWoD lines, 1 Exalted, 4 publisher owned lines, 2 creator owned lines, and 1 d20 line.* There's no way that I'm going to enjoy or appreciate all of those! (I don't.) That said, there's no reason for me to get upset when OP writers decide to develop ideas that some of their audience has shown interest in. That's not Stepford politeness. I don't see the point in grousing publicly about creative ideas I'm not into. Still, I'm totally on board with speculating about how to hack or change the setting in various directions.<br /> <br /> *I probably miscounted. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T21:24:58-07:00","id":481910,"title":"","content":"I mean, if you want a developer to listen to your criticisms you're gonna have to present it in an even more constructive and positive manner than to get us forum-posters to listen. We're just fans, we didn't create the damn games. Going back to the OP of this thread, what is a developer to do with &quot;I absolutely hate this concept?&quot; If enough people hate the concept to make a difference in Onyx Path's bottom line, then it'll show in the sales numbers, and there's still no use in pure negativity.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>I would go so far as saying that negativity directed at the product, rather than the producers, is a vitally important part of any creative process. </i>&quot;<br /> I disagree. Criticism yes, but negativity, no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5697,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","user":"n_a_anyon","date":". 04-16-2015, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","name":"n_a_anyon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T22:10:16-07:00","id":481937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>n_a_anyon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481910#post481910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if you want a developer to listen to your criticisms you're gonna have to present it in an even more constructive and positive manner than to get us forum-posters to listen. We're just fans, we didn't create the damn games. Going back to the OP of this thread, what is a developer to do with &quot;I absolutely hate this concept?&quot; If enough people hate the concept to make a difference in Onyx Path's bottom line, then it'll show in the sales numbers, and there's still no use in pure negativity.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>I would go so far as saying that negativity directed at the product, rather than the producers, is a vitally important part of any creative process. </i>&quot;<br /> I disagree. Criticism yes, but negativity, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that short of direct emails, these forums are one of the easiest ways to address the devs themselves. Not to mention that by expressing concerns on these forums they can be discussed in ways that might clarify worries born of misunderstanding.<br /> <br /> And the line between negativity and criticism is a very fine one. What you saw as negativity I saw as criticism, but chose to use your own language in replying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481795#post481795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've also literally compared your own disagreement with set elements of the core mechanics to disagreeing with <i>fascism</i>, so I feel as though there's a very large middle ground being excluded here in the name of hyperbole.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall ever doing that, so would appreciate a refresher course if you are going to make this personal and bring past conversations into this. Regardless, even if contextually true, I don't see how that has any bearing on my most recent post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481821#post481821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one's silencing you or other dissenting opinions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>n_a_anyon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481483#post481483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No offense to you personally Magnum Opus, but that's exactly the type of negative post I think these boards could do without.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is what I was directly replying to. Magnum Opus' comment wasn't particularly negative, nor was he asking for a rollback and trashing of the Godmachine Chronicles as a quality book unto itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","user":"Anachronistic Jam","date":". 04-16-2015, 01:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T22:55:59-07:00","id":481975,"title":"","content":"In the interests of consolidation and getting this thread back on something resembling a track, can some people more familiar with the corpus of DtF/cDemon sum up the antagonist situation of that line for the thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T23:11:14-07:00","id":481984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481975#post481975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the interests of consolidation and getting this thread back on something resembling a track, can some people more familiar with the corpus of DtF/cDemon sum up the antagonist situation of that line for the thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the oddest things about Demon the Fallen was that when the protagonist demons clawed their way out of hell and into human bodies, God and his Angels were nowhere to be seen, and the Apocalypse (late 90s, early 2000s) seemed to be nigh anyway. Because of the fact that the protagonists, who were the weakest of the fallen host, merged with dying, dead, or otherwise checked out human beings, they gained a measure of sanity and respite from the torments of hell. The same was not true of their enemies, the Earthbound.<br /> <br /> Long ago, the most powerful lords of hell were summoned to earth, possibly by Lucifer and in some cases by diabolist magi, and were bound into physical objects, such as idols. These Earthbound had already been driven mad by both their actions during the War and by the torments of hell. They began to manipulate humans, sometimes taking the guise of various gods in order to siphon prayers, faith, and devotion away from them. <br /> <br /> The protagonist demons oppose the Earthbound for a variety of reasons. One is merely that the protagonists don't wish to be controlled by the Earthbound. Other protagonist demons have rediscovered their love for humanity and fears the ill intent the Earthbound have toward them. <br /> <br /> In Demon: the Descent, the spiritual successors to the Earthbound are the Exiles - angels who lost their connection to the God-Machine without falling. They can be incredibly ancient, and they have to go to great and bizarre lengths to keep themselves from going dormant for lack of essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T23:25:26-07:00","id":482040,"title":"","content":"Well, to start you had the 'standard' enemy of many World of Darkness games, other members of your own kind. There was a lot of different beliefs among the demons about what happened and how they should deal with it, and while disagreements didn't always lead to antagonism, they could. Plus there were demons out there who wanted to damn it all, they hadn't been anchored in the right kind of human soul like everyone else, didn't calm their Torment and were just driven by anguish and hatred, their time locked in the senseless Abyss for however long didn't soothe them.<br /> <br /> There's similarities between the factions of the Fallen and the agendas of the Descended, but they also overlap a bit with other lines, like Changeling, as they answer the question of, 'What is your character after?'<br /> <br /> Then there were my favorites, the Earthbound. You sort of have an idigam thing going here. The Earthbound were taken from the Pit earlier, and rather than having souls to ground them exist in reliquaries. They are powerful, corrupting forces that relish in worship and eeeeeevil.<br /> <br /> There's also a wide variety of mortal enemies, either those who didn't believe demons had a place in the world or hunters or the minions of other demons or Earthbound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T01:10:57-07:00","id":482117,"title":"","content":"I know nothing about Demon the Fallen, but I do very much like the kind of spiritual horror inspired by the traditional notion of demons and think they deserve a place in nWoD. There seems to me to be a lot more room for lower-case-d demons than just importing ideas from DtF. EDIT: Duh-doy, I forgot about the WoD: Inferno book. What's people's opinions on that?<br /> <br /> My final words on negativity vs criticism:<br /> I think I interpreted some statements as more negative than they were intended. I was thrown off by the &quot;getting rid of&quot; wording which Magnum then clarified. The line between criticism and negativity is indeed thin, I suppose, but that makes it all the more important to make sure one is clear in how they communicate. My point wasn't that people shouldn't post their opinions on these forums, both positive and negative, but that if you want to have someone listen to your negative opinion, ESPECIALLY someone who was creatively involved in the thing you don't totally like, you better make sure you're saying something of substance, otherwise you'll get ignored at best and flamed at worst. And you better make sure you actually know what you're talking about.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5697,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","user":"n_a_anyon","date":". 04-16-2015, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","name":"n_a_anyon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T06:16:24-07:00","id":482267,"title":"","content":"My issue with Demon the Fallen and more of world of darkness classic is that Christianity was Right, and all other religions were empirically Wrong. There was a war against God, there was a Cain, there was a Great Flood. The God Machine could or not be God, and some religions may or may not have been related, but it's not Known.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T06:29:47-07:00","id":482271,"title":"","content":"Well, there was always the Gaia thing. Which I guess is just one more reason crossovers were a bit difficult. Christianity is as solidly wrong in Werewolf the Apocalypse and Mage the Ascention (I think) as it is right everywhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T06:34:56-07:00","id":482273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=482271#post482271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there was always the Gaia thing. Which I guess is just one more reason crossovers were a bit difficult. Christianity is as solidly wrong in Werewolf the Apocalypse and Mage the Ascention (I think) as it is right everywhere else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Demon: the Fallen references that there used to be multiple layers of reality. In one, Angels were just natural laws, and in another they were divinely powered, winged beings personally responsible for creation. When they see the Werewolves, they wonder if they're reincarnation of warrior angels. They might have even been right, back when there were several layers of reality. It's implied that at some point, everything messily collapsed to one layer, likely populated by unwitting refugees from multiple layers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T08:24:38-07:00","id":482390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481353#post481353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can make your counterargument without engaging in such an obnoxious break in character. Reasons to be disgusted with people are not an appreciated gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry you don't appreciate my sense of humor; and that's all the apology you're going to get, as I've done nothing to warrant any more of one. <i>I'd</i> appreciate you not jumping down my throat just because I chose to use a bit of levity: if you have an issue with me, report me or contact me privately. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481353#post481353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">]Chapter full of Bound widgets aside, it presents a distinctly different take on the Underworld to what <i>Geist</i> does. <i>The Book of Spirits</i> does not have a comparable <i>Werewolf</i> section and shares BotD's &quot;the realm in mortal consciousness&quot; style of first chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last I checked, Book of the Dead's portrayal of the Underworld is a direct extrapolation of Geist's portrayal of the Underworld. Which is not surprising, as the two were designed together. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481353#post481353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're sending some mixed messages here with this terrible basic-sarcasm thing you're doing, seeing as this is explicitly false by virtue of the &quot;Next Book&quot; blurb in <i>Witch Finders</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed I am sending mixed messages; because part of my point is that whether something is a &quot;blue book supplement&quot; or a supplement of a particular gameline isn't always clear cut. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481353#post481353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As has been highlighted, this one's just a statement of fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, Skinchangers got advertised in a &quot;Next Book&quot; blurb of one of the Werewolf supplements (though I forget which one). It was, after all, designed to be a Werewolf supplement right up to the eleventh hour, and was retrofitted as a &quot;blue book&quot; supplement as it was about to go to print. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481361#post481361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is that <i>Slasher</i> is blatantly and observably in a different boat than the others and that calling it a Hunter supplement is <i>especially</i> different from calling the GMC a &quot;supplement&quot; for a gameline that <i>didn't come out until over half a year after the rules update did.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I never said that GMC <i>is</i> a supplement for <b>Demon</b>; only that I'd like it to be rebranded as such. If you're going to take issue with what I said, take issue with what I <i>said</i>, not with a misrepresentation of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T08:39:04-07:00","id":482423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>n_a_anyon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=482117#post482117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forgot about the WoD: Inferno book. What's people's opinions on that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not speaking for everyone but I loved it. It's probably my favorite of the minor template books, and I think it's easier to use in major template games. I have heard some people not liking it, or complaining about 'power levels' but most of those I've spoken to like it very much.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T09:09:14-07:00","id":482443,"title":"","content":"Of course, the GMC rules kinda pulled the rug from under a couple of mechanics it relies on quite heavily (morality, plus to a lesser extent virtues and vices)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T09:54:09-07:00","id":482481,"title":"","content":"GMC rules added affectations from FATE to the game. This expanded the experience system into something that was more Story driven and Story driving. The adaptation granted a wider range of motives, temperament, and personality facets to characters.<br /> <br /> That being said, I have had a similar difficulty with NWoD rules as did the OP. The new systems are in my opinion a more refined gaming mechanic. However, the pretense that each game comes without an implied Meta simply doesn't work. Each of them carries an implied Meta which unfolds in the flavor of the motifs and political divisions offered. The classic meta can be imposed - and I prefer that Meta for both opportunity and consistency. The Classic Meta unified the cosmogonic expressions of the entire world. What I see here is a strong division between those for whom existence is non-differentiated and secular and those for whom existence is differentiated and full of sacrality's influence. The former will never sense the disharmony of the Platonic spheres which the latter find incongruous to their &quot;golden ratio&quot; providing the fundament of beingness. Yes this is a very esoteric description. The GMC creates a Meta for NWoD that is counter-intuitive to, even pejorative of, the spiritual experience. Classic incorporated not merely an affectation, but an effectivity for both dogma and praxis from even the most opposed traditional view points while allowing neo-gens secular unawareness of the cosmogonic around them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T10:13:16-07:00","id":482500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=482443#post482443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, the GMC rules kinda pulled the rug from under a couple of mechanics it relies on quite heavily (morality, plus to a lesser extent virtues and vices)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one of the more salient disjunctions is the completely different Influence caps, honestly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=481984#post481984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the oddest things about Demon the Fallen was that when the protagonist demons clawed their way out of hell and into human bodies, God and his Angels were nowhere to be seen, and the Apocalypse (late 90s, early 2000s) seemed to be nigh anyway. Because of the fact that the protagonists, who were the weakest of the fallen host, merged with dying, dead, or otherwise checked out human beings, they gained a measure of sanity and respite from the torments of hell. The same was not true of their enemies, the Earthbound.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> In Demon: the Descent, the spiritual successors to the Earthbound are the Exiles - angels who lost their connection to the God-Machine without falling. They can be incredibly ancient, and they have to go to great and bizarre lengths to keep themselves from going dormant for lack of essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't sure whether I had overlooked something when I couldn't find/remember non-Fallen angels in my few brief forays into cDemon's material, so it's good to get confirmation of that.<br /> <br /> The fact that the Unchained draw their starting demonic forms from their angelic forms (which run across the whole demonic/angelic spectrum) and have a looser standard of Virtue and Vice seems like it can be leaned upon in attempting to emulate Fallen's demons; ditto one of the common Integrator views of Hell in combination with some exiles being warped in mind and/or body due to flaws in their summoning.<br /> <br /> Bumping up the God-Machine's degree of secrecy, incorporating the book's suggestion for introducing the Unchained into a running game via broken storage/transport facilities, and leaning on the idea that someone on the old forums brought up that the Machine is something made to do an undesirable job (which itself has resonance in the Idealists' true divinity movement) could go a ways toward evoking Fallen's take on God.<br /> <br /> Any other notable facets of the games' points of interface come to mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T10:17:00-07:00","id":482504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=482481#post482481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The classic meta can be imposed - and I prefer that Meta for both opportunity and consistency. The Classic Meta unified the cosmogonic expressions of the entire world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel pretty confident in saying that neither cWoD, nWoD 1E, or nWoD 2E has had a unified cosmology. Each individual line (cMage, nMage, cDemon, nDemon, etc) has its own themes, many of which touch on different and sometimes contradictory forms of spirituality and parts of the human experience.<br /> <br /> I think it's an error to consider the GMC a sort of overarching canon in the nWoD that has spiritual implications for the whole universe. The nWoD is mechanically and thematically modular, and the GMC is made up of a lot of different story elements and ideas that can add to a game. None of them are mandatory. The book shies away from presenting even a canon version of itself, instead providing multiple possible origins and reasons for existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 04-16-2015, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T12:32:26-07:00","id":482639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=482504#post482504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel pretty confident in saying that neither cWoD, nWoD 1E, or nWoD 2E has had a unified cosmology. Each individual line (cMage, nMage, cDemon, nDemon, etc) has its own themes, many of which touch on different and sometimes contradictory forms of spirituality and parts of the human experience.<br /> <br /> I think it's an error to consider the GMC a sort of overarching canon in the nWoD that has spiritual implications for the whole universe. The nWoD is mechanically and thematically modular, and the GMC is made up of a lot of different story elements and ideas that can add to a game. None of them are mandatory. The book shies away from presenting even a canon version of itself, instead providing multiple possible origins and reasons for existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This over 9000!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T14:45:34-07:00","id":482831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=482500#post482500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think one of the more salient disjunctions is the completely different Influence caps, honestly.<br /> <br /> <br /> I wasn't sure whether I had overlooked something when I couldn't find/remember non-Fallen angels in my few brief forays into cDemon's material, so it's good to get confirmation of that.<br /> <br /> The fact that the Unchained draw their starting demonic forms from their angelic forms (which run across the whole demonic/angelic spectrum) and have a looser standard of Virtue and Vice seems like it can be leaned upon in attempting to emulate Fallen's demons; ditto one of the common Integrator views of Hell in combination with some exiles being warped in mind and/or body due to flaws in their summoning.<br /> <br /> Bumping up the God-Machine's degree of secrecy, incorporating the book's suggestion for introducing the Unchained into a running game via broken storage/transport facilities, and leaning on the idea that someone on the old forums brought up that the Machine is something made to do an undesirable job (which itself has resonance in the Idealists' true divinity movement) could go a ways toward evoking Fallen's take on God.<br /> <br /> Any other notable facets of the games' points of interface come to mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Agendas are very similar to the Factions of the fallen. <br /> <br /> DTD Agendas:<br /> <b>Integrator </b>- Rejoin the God-Machine on one's own terms.<br /> <b>Saboteur </b>- Blow up God.<br /> <b>Inquisitor </b>- Find out what the G-M is up to.<br /> <b>Tempter </b>- Forget the G-M, build an awesome existence right here.<br /> <br /> DTF Factions<br /> <b>Faustian</b> - Exploit humankind for one's own benefit. (A bit similar to Tempter)<br /> <b>Cryptic</b> - Figure out Lucifer and God's secret plans. (Much like Inquisitor)<br /> <b>Luciferan</b> - Find Satan, rejoin him, defeat God. (Kinda like Saboteur)<br /> <b>Ravener</b> - Destroy all of the works of God, including humans (No real analog)<br /> <b>Reconciler</b> - Gain forgiveness from God. (Similar to Integrator)<br /> <br /> Another thing that's similar is the necessity of Pacts. DTF demons need pacts to sustain themselves with Faith. In return, they grant humans access to their powers. DTD demons need pacts and souls in order to hide from the G-M. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T18:07:10-07:00","id":483005,"title":"","content":"I'd say that the Ravager faction is a better parallel to the Saboteur Agenda than the Luciferans are; the latter don't have a counterpart in Descent because Descent doesn't have a counterpart to Lucifer. <br /> <br /> A major difference between the two games is that the God of the Fallen is, at worst, an absentee landlord, and is very easy to portray sympathetically (making the Reconcilers a very attractive faction); meanwhile, the God-Machine of the Descent is very <i>difficult</i> to portray sympathetically, as it is by default an inhuman tyrant who hunts down and destroys former agents who dare think for themselves and views humans either as cogs in the machine or as utterly unimportant. This makes the Integrators one of the <i>least</i> attractive of the Agendas, and only playable (IMHO) as &quot;rejoin the God-Machine in order to change it from within&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T19:25:33-07:00","id":483084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=483005#post483005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes the Integrators one of the <i>least</i> attractive of the Agendas, and only playable (IMHO) as &quot;rejoin the God-Machine in order to change it from within&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's their role, though. If you just wanted to rejoin it as it is, you'd be killing yourself. It's compelling in a different way from &quot;well maybe God isn't such a bad guy.&quot; It's about reconciling with how things used to be, or recognizing the potential in a thing like the God-Machine. What if you could take control, and use it to make things better? And so on.<br /> <br /> They're not identical, and for very good reasons. Integrators are particularly constructed for a God-Machine mythos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T22:54:50-07:00","id":483219,"title":"","content":"Also Interrogators may not have fallen by their own choices. It could be someone who wishes things had never changed but now that they have free will they are conflicted because they don't want to die but they want to return to how things once were. Imagine them more as 18 year old kids who were just kicked out and know nothing about the world and look upon their memories with nostalgia despite the fact of what would happen if they came back home.<br /> <br /> Actually on that tangent compare them to a kid who was kicked out because they were gay and they were threatened &quot;if you ever come back...&quot; yet they still dream of their childhood and how nice things were. They deep down want to go back to how things were before something not in their control destroyed everything. If they could just find someway to return to their happy life from before they'd do anything but they haven't so their fear makes them hide. Death may be a tempting release but they fight through it. Their friends who were kicked out as well may ridicule the interrogator for wanting to go back but it doesn't change how things are. Maybe they come up with a plan to change their father's mind and they think that this is the plan that will let them return home, living as they fondly remember.<br /> <br /> *Note, though I was in the closet at one time I did not go through the above. I am just able to best frame it as such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T04:08:44-07:00","id":483401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Satchel:</b> And in case those people ever <i>actually show up,</i> they will get just as much of my scorn as the multifarious Chicken Littles that are presently making nuisances of themselves warning against the specter of Mage Supremacy or Deus Est Machina Uber Alles. </div> </div> </div>Huh. It's usually me saying things like that. Nice to know I'm not the only one. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Dataweaver:</b> I'd like God-Machine Chronicle to be rebranded as a Demon supplement. I don't want anything that would give the impression that the God-Machine is in any way central to the World of Darkness. </div> </div> </div>I'm torn on that. It's central enough to Demon that the case for having it just there is obvious. On the other hand, it's a good enemy for a human chronicle. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd rather see a selection of monsters that don't fit neatly into any of the boxes that the existing gamelines have established \u2014 essentially a blue-book version of the Night Horrors concept. </div> </div> </div>Some of the monsters from Antagonists would do well in this role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T06:45:26-07:00","id":483508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=483401#post483401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm torn on that. It's central enough to Demon that the case for having it just there is obvious. On the other hand, it's a good enemy for a human chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is what GMC is, it's options for mortal chronicles, it's barely Demon related at all. It has Angels and cult antagonists, mysteries for mortals to fit into and solve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-17-2015, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T07:30:54-07:00","id":483527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=483401#post483401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm torn on that. It's central enough to Demon that the case for having it just there is obvious. On the other hand, it's a good enemy for a human chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that\u2019s true of virtually every antagonist type I can think of. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=483508#post483508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is what GMC is, it's options for mortal chronicles, it's barely Demon related at all. It has Angels and cult antagonists, mysteries for mortals to fit into and solve.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that I've been talking in terms of \u201cshould be\u201d, not \u201cis\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T08:30:46-07:00","id":483549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=483508#post483508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is what GMC is, it's options for mortal chronicles, it's barely Demon related at all. It has Angels and cult antagonists, mysteries for mortals to fit into and solve.</div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed. Though, with a caveat. The Shadow is primarily a Werewolf thing, the Underworld is primarily a Geist thing; other games can dabble there (especially mortals), though, and both got covered with a Book. I think of GMC as just another Book of Spirits, but for angels and with a different name. <br /> <br /> So, the God-Machine is primarily a Demon thing, though I expect others to dabble, and the mortals get a general book to play with. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T20:32:14-07:00","id":484206,"title":"","content":"In the Principle vs God Machine vs Empyrean vs whatever argument, am I the only one that takes the Ugaritic Text approach?<br /> They are all Gods battling it out for supremacy.<br /> <br /> I got interesting Ideas for El Shaddai.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T20:49:08-07:00","id":484213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=484206#post484206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Principle vs God Machine vs Empyrean vs whatever argument, am I the only one that takes the Ugaritic Text approach?<br /> They are all Gods battling it out for supremacy.<br /> <br /> I got interesting Ideas for El Shaddai.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny, I had a scene in a Descent game between Anpu and a demon that basically described the world as a variant of this.<br /> <br /> It was more how certain gods like the Machine and the Exarchs feel a need to subjugate all others, and the others, like the Nameless Beasts or Luna, who were more than happy to spend some time swatting them down for their ideas, but either way it builds up to the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T21:02:04-07:00","id":484225,"title":"","content":"On Demon: the Fallen chat - and it's been a long, long time so I could be way off base here - I think it's a mistake to categorize Earthbound as the line's main antagonists. The main antagonists in D:tF are demons, and I don't mean quite in the same way that vampires have to deal with other vampires. The protagonists are assumed to be part of the group of Demons that, upon taking a new body, were shocked out of their hellish ways by their host's remnants of humanity, becoming a mix of the demon they are, the angel they were and the human they took over. The vast majority of demons that now have bodies did <i>not</i> experience this moment of clarity and are still the twisted, tormented monsters that dwelled in Hell for so very, very long and they want to spread the suffering..<br /> <br /> My opinion on nWoD stuff is entirely unoriginal: I encourage people to treat the fluff as a toolkit to be used as much or as little as you want for your individual games. I like hammering cosmologies together, which is why for my Demon game the God-Machine's origins very directly involve the Exarchs and the Principle and indirectly reference the gods of the Shadow and the Others from Arcadia, but I also have a cosmology for games that only involve Vampire/Geist/Promethean/Mummy with a heavy emphasis on the Inferno supplement. As much as cosmology wank is fun - and it's so much fun - the only time I think you're obligated to have any mention of the God-Machine around is when you're playing Demon*. Otherwise, it's all up in the air for each campaign.<br /> <br /> * I'm sure there's also probably a way to play Demon without the G-M but at that point you're putting in a lot of work for little gain, IMO, so I have no really good advice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 04-18-2015, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T22:13:15-07:00","id":484278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=484225#post484225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* I'm sure there's also probably a way to play Demon without the G-M but at that point you're putting in a lot of work for little gain, IMO, so I have no really good advice.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty easy. Make God distant, unreactive, and not particularly invasive. Embeds and Exploits still work - they're just tricks built into the system. The great part about the Machine is that it's unclear if it created anything or if it's just there taking advantage of what's already in place, or, honestly, if it's even <i>real</i>. What if demons are just really schizophrenic fragments of the Akashic record?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T23:07:24-07:00","id":484309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=484278#post484278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The great part about the Machine is that it's unclear if it created anything or if it's just there taking advantage of what's already in place, or, honestly, if it's even <i>real</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, let's stop a moment and look half-objectively at the forces the Machine holds an analogous position to in their own gamelines. You have\u2026<ul><li>The fact of transformation and consequence, poetically and sometimes literally expressed as the most volatile classical element and other sources of power.</li> <li>The fundamental web of interconnection between all things as manifest in emergent storybook patterns in the rational and irrational presentations of un/reality.</li> <li>The incomprehensibly vast social organism that reflects things of mystical-emotional potency in the world and the strange collection of laws and customs that feed and bind them.</li> <li>The giant nightmarish passion-pit of dead gods and port cities on the rivers to What Comes Next, which occasionally reaches up to steer entire cultures or troubleshoot mortality.</li> </ul><br /> &quot;The Questionably-Unified Theory of Magic Science, Occasionally Wearing the Hat What Has Gears On&quot; isn't exactly a weird standout System in that thematic lineup of Agent-Dispatching Principals, and if you can scale a game of Geist or Werewolf back to reduce the amount of interface with the Shadow or the Underworld in favor of Supernatural PVP you can certainly do the same with Demon and the Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T07:49:13-07:00","id":484547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My opinion on nWoD stuff is entirely unoriginal: I encourage people to treat the fluff as a toolkit to be used as much or as little as you want for your individual games. I like hammering cosmologies together, which is why for my Demon game the God-Machine's origins very directly involve the Exarchs and the Principle and indirectly reference the gods of the Shadow and the Others from Arcadia, but I also have a cosmology for games that only involve Vampire/Geist/Promethean/Mummy with a heavy emphasis on the Inferno supplement. As much as cosmology wank is fun - and it's so much fun - the only time I think you're obligated to have any mention of the God-Machine around is when you're playing Demon*. Otherwise, it's all up in the air for each campaign. </div> </div> </div>I'm the exact opposite I think an over reliance on perceived &quot;judeo/christian&quot; myth is boring.<br /> Only exception was the 7 virtues / vices and I am sad it is gone in Vampire.<br /> After all what most people think they know of Hell and Demons is apocryphal anyway.<br /> <br /> From what I know of the GMC is a fresh quasi chthonic take on the whole matter.<br /> Same with the Principle and the Quashmallen, very mysterious.<br /> If the old testament god shows up at all in my world it will be as the demiurge.<br /> <br /> As the ex priest cop state in prophecy states, when angels show up it is always bad news.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T08:02:22-07:00","id":484568,"title":"","content":"Worth noting: at no point did I say you should rely on the Judeo-Christian God if you don't use the God-Machine; on the contrary, besides the role He plays in modern religion I usually leave the idea of &quot;God&quot; alone.<br /> <br /> Running oVamp or oDemon is a different story entirely, but that's not what we're talking about anyways.<br /> <br /> Edit: In fact, the closest I come to touching on the presence of God is in the grand unified backstory I am working on for a lot of my home games, and here it is: at the dawn of reality, many, many iterations ago, the God-Machine and the Principle were one force dedicated to protecting and enforcing causality. -Someone or something- might have needed to create such a mechanism before the dawn of time itself, but there is no other evidence of such a force existing or being able to exist before reality itself. -If- it existed, it might be God. Or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 04-18-2015, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T17:07:41-07:00","id":488849,"title":"","content":"I have to say, the discussion about science being a process of understanding, not a list of yeses and nos, warmed my heart to no end <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T09:19:34-07:00","id":872432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=465706#post465706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your complaint is vague, your terminology is poorly defined, and your opinion is utterly irrelevant to the reasonable thing you are asking after, all of which is business as usual for this type of discussion, which has been had multiple times with an overabundance of vitriol.<br /> <br /> Literally the only thing you had to do was ask if there was a Translation Guide in the works for Demon: the Fallen, as there has been one for Vampire: the Masquerade, Werewolf: the Apocalypse, and Mage: the Ascension; as has been highlighted above, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198652-demon-translation-guide\">there is indeed a DtF/DtD Translation Guide being written</a>, and as highlighted above, there is no force employed by Onyx Path Publishing that can cause you to play Demon: the Descent against your will.*<br /> <br /> * I would put a jocularly menacing &quot;<i>Yet.</i>&quot; here, but experience suggests this is an unwise line of frivolity to pursue.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ugh. Replies like this are what give the gaming community 1) drama 2) bad reputations. There's nothing wrong with the OP's question, or how it was presented, and the answer of &quot;just ask for a translation guide&quot; amounts to the worst answer possible.<br /> <br /> I agree with the OP. At times the &quot;God Machine&quot; does not fit a game thematically. Using it breaks immersion and degrades the game. So, taking advice, I purchased the translation guide, which was worthless. All it did was give advice on converting a character from one setting to the other. Nothing on actually removing the God Machine or what to replace it with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1907-waywardson74","name":"Waywardson74","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T09:37:08-07:00","id":872447,"title":"","content":"Does thread necromancy mean nothing anymore?<br /> <br /> I'd ask why you're kicking a dead horse, but it's the pastime here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T09:37:38-07:00","id":872449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Waywardson74</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=872432#post872432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing wrong with the OP's question, or how it was presented, and the answer of &quot;just ask for a translation guide&quot; amounts to the worst answer possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>He made a thread about Demon: the Descent to ask how to <i>not use it</i>, a process which is as simple as <i>not using it</i>.<br /> <br /> The implicit-demand-masquerading-as-a-question of &quot;are there plans to replace this gameline with a gameline from a completely separate setting because I don't like a major element of this gameline?&quot; has more problems than I care to find a stick to shake at.<br /> <br /> This place was the New World of Darkness forum when this thread was first created and last posted in <i>a year ago</i> seriously what are you doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T09:42:02-07:00","id":872452,"title":"","content":"I wonder what this act of necromancy nets as a bonus to Ceremonies. It's got to be at least a +2. The deathly energies feel thick in the aether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T10:36:04-07:00","id":872484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=872452#post872452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder what this act of necromancy nets as a bonus to Ceremonies. It's got to be at least a +2. The deathly energies feel thick in the aether.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone's already thinking about their yantras.<br /> <br /> Obligatory:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/VcAnC.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T10:44:32-07:00","id":872495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=872484#post872484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Someone's already thinking about their yantras.<br /> <br /> Obligatory:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/VcAnC.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a Sin-Eater comment, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","