rcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T12:07:42-07:00","id":872573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=872449#post872449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He made a thread about Demon: the Descent to ask how to <i>not use it</i>, a process which is as simple as <i>not using it</i>.<br /> <br /> The implicit-demand-masquerading-as-a-question of &quot;are there plans to replace this gameline with a gameline from a completely separate setting because I don't like a major element of this gameline?&quot; has more problems than I care to find a stick to shake at.<br /> <br /> This place was the New World of Darkness forum when this thread was first created and last posted in <i>a year ago</i> seriously what are you doing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, you misread what they were asking. They didn't ask how not to use Demon the Descent while playing Demon the Descent, they asked how not to use the God Machine.<br /> <br /> What am I doing? Looking for ideas on that same thought, and finding you being a douche to another member of the community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1907-waywardson74","name":"Waywardson74","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T12:14:27-07:00","id":872582,"title":"","content":"Can we avoid the name-calling, dude? It's unnecessary and definitely doesn't help the level of dialogue in the thread.<br /> <br /> I think you need to phrase it more substantially. The Demon Translation Guide gives some thoughts on using the Abrahamic God from Fallen IIRC, but I'm not certain I can follow what you actually want. Do you want there to be no God-thing at all, or do you want a God that isn't the Machine? If you're expecting serious help it'd be worth clarifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T12:19:24-07:00","id":872586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Waywardson74</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=872573#post872573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, you misread what they were asking. They didn't ask how not to use Demon the Descent while playing Demon the Descent, they asked how not to use the God Machine.<br /> <br /> What am I doing? Looking for ideas on that same thought, and finding you being a douche to another member of the community.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the first post openly asks &quot;How do I play Demon the Fallen in nWoD? with a very shaky progression of events from there, at best. Really, there was no reason to bring up Demon the Descent at all, and yet he did, with apparently no other purpose than expressing dislike for Descent, which is rather unnecessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T12:23:21-07:00","id":872587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Waywardson74</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=872573#post872573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, you misread what they were asking. They didn't ask how not to use Demon the Descent while playing Demon the Descent, they asked how not to use the God Machine.<br /> <br /> What am I doing? Looking for ideas on that same thought, and finding you being a douche to another member of the community.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">Granted, some of us, myself included, came of somewhat abrasively in the beginning of this thread, which was over a year ago. That does not make it okay to make personal attacks against those users. I'm only giving you a warning for now because you are new to these forums, but you should know that we take personal attacks and group attacks very seriously.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T14:31:48-07:00","id":872643,"title":"","content":"But anyways, it must be said again that Demon the Fallen or Inferno tend to fill the niches for most of the people who don't like Descent's techgnosticism. The Translation game lets you use Fallen in a ChroD system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T18:12:15-07:00","id":872776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=872529#post872529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What always tripped me up was the descriptions of angels being physically taken apart; parts exchanged, and up-kept like machines. Angels are luminous beings naturally, so it seems incongruous to me. But, maybe that is just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a little pressed for time and bandwidth at present, but: Arc mentioned metaphors earlier re: angels as Twilight entities.<br /> <br /> The Fall renders an angel naturally material \u2014 who all remembers learning about electron shells in science class?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T18:26:44-07:00","id":872783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=872776#post872776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fall renders an angel naturally material \u2014 who all remembers learning about electron shells in science class?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but they have no use here. Unless someone wants to argue that being corporeal is a lower energy state than Twilight beings. It's a metaphor that quickly collapses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T19:09:04-07:00","id":872804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=872587#post872587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:red\">Granted, some of us, myself included, came of somewhat abrasively in the beginning of this thread, which was over a year ago. That does not make it okay to make personal attacks against those users. I'm only giving you a warning for now because you are new to these forums, but you should know that we take personal attacks and group attacks very seriously.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Not to white knight here, but what'd he even do though? He said he thought Satchel acted like a douche towards someone (which to me is like saying cats meow) while noting how for a thread asking about ideas on porting Fallen over to nWoD due to a personal dislike for Descent had so much &quot;BLASPHEMY&quot; going on towards the OP that had the audacity to not like the same thing, whatever his reasons, that I had to take a break between reading the first page alone and wind down my misanthropy before I could pick it up again just to see if anyone down the line would take a calm breath and try and do something to help the guy, whatever disagreements with his views aside, other than &quot;buy the new supplement that'll be out sometime soon lelelel;&quot; which is exactly what happened in the thread until about page 3 or so.<br /> <br /> Noting someone is acting in a condescending better-than-thou by saying the way they act is douchey, one of the tamest of insults that isn't even worth calling a swear word, is in my opinion not worth a warning from a moderator as if he said &quot;here's a tip, cunt; your IQ will raise if you scoop up a handful of shit from the local wildlife and put it where other people have brains;&quot; that's a personal attack worthy of a &quot;jesus tone down dude.&quot; Maybe it's just me and I don't mean to say you're doing a bad job as a moderator- don't get me wrong -but I really think freedom of speech gets a slap on the wrist when you hand out warnings under the moderator banner for using really tame language to call someone's behaviour out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T20:11:46-07:00","id":872830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=872783#post872783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes but they have no use here. Unless someone wants to argue that being corporeal is a lower energy state than Twilight beings. It's a metaphor that quickly collapses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not seeing the point at which the collapse occurs. Unpack, please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T20:46:43-07:00","id":872847,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7060_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7060\" data-vbnamecard=\"7060\">Karavolos</a> Go check out the TOU here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T22:20:23-07:00","id":872890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=872804#post872804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but I really think freedom of speech gets a slap on the wrist when you hand out warnings under the moderator banner for using really tame language to call someone's behaviour out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only responding to this specific part because it's a bugbear of mine: freedom of speech is a very specific thing and doesn't cover the Terms of Use on a private internet board.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T22:51:11-07:00","id":872905,"title":"","content":"So much for quietly forgetting this thread exists.<br /> <br /> I should probably ignore this, but if this is still going tomorrow, I'll respond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T03:41:45-07:00","id":873001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=872804#post872804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really think freedom of speech gets a slap on the wrist when you hand out warnings under the moderator banner for using really tame language to call someone's behaviour out.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#ff0000\">\u200bYou need to understand that when you use a privately owned forum there is no &quot;freedom of speech&quot;, you either conform to the standards set by the owners of the site or you don't get to continue posting on that site. You do not have the right or privilege of posting whatever you wish in any manner you wish. If the moderators warn someone that their language and attitude is unacceptable then that's what it is. If they continue to post in that manner then their privilege to post is rescinded. Different people have different levels of tolerance for insults and aggressive behavior, we set a minimum acceptable level of behavior and if one can't abide by that then they should find somewhere else to post. If you or anyone else has an issue with a statement posted on the forum then the proper procedure is to report it and move on, not make comments directed at the person making the offending post. The moderation staff has the job of determining if there was a rules violation that is actionable, no one else does. Calling someone a douche or saying they are acting like one is a rules violation and if Charlaquin hadn't already addressed it I would have, much less leniently.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 04-24-2016, 06:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T06:45:12-07:00","id":873058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=872804#post872804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...(which to me is like saying cats meow)...</div> </div> </div> </div>Um. I laughed.<br /> <br /> I had a quibble with Satchel...I guess a couple years ago now? With that said, they're probably, in my mind, straight up the most knowledgeable person on these forums regarding the game-lines","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T07:07:04-07:00","id":873068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=872905#post872905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So much for quietly forgetting this thread exists.<br /> <br /> I should probably ignore this, but if this is still going tomorrow, I'll respond.</div> </div> </div> </div>Show true wisdom and walk away.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T07:13:52-07:00","id":873070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=872830#post872830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not seeing the point at which the collapse occurs. Unpack, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>Check your high school chemistry book again. The metaphor breaks down at multiple points. When you're positive that you can't find any of them, then check back with me again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T07:36:29-07:00","id":873078,"title":"","content":"I must say I don't understand why does the angel's &quot;state of being&quot; could be a problem for the machine metaphor- nothing stops you from ripping Twilight beings into shreds, considering that you have the right tools for the mission. Mechanism is a concept- you could call a collection of few molecules a &quot;machine&quot;, as long as they do what a machine is meant to do- taking raw materials and creating a product. Your cells are made of biological machines, which work constantly to keep you alive. Modern chemists work on nano technology for drugs as some sort of miniature machines. I can't see why the fact that angels are not naturally physical should, by any means, turned them into less &quot;mechanical&quot;, just because they exist in the Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T08:59:08-07:00","id":873120,"title":"","content":"The metaphor that doesn't work is electron energy states one. But also the use of machine imagery on the whole is more thematic than metaphorical. It's the thing that links Demons to Angels to the God-Machine. It's a factor they have in common and that commonality primarily serves a thematic purpose.<br /> <br /> With respect to whether or not whatever aspect of machine imagery is actually a metaphor and whether or not it works depends on the authors' original intentions. IMO, the goal is probably to showcase a supreme entity that is so alien that its motives are unknowable. The fact that the imagery of machines is used as opposed to the more anthropomorphic representations that are more commonly attributed to deities and their minions (and their opponents) seems to support such an interpretation. If that was the goal, to showcase the alien aspect of the God-Machine and the continuum of things related to it through shared thematic imagery (i.e. angels, infrastructure, and demons), then that metaphorical usage begins to breakdown as soon as counter-examples to that alienness, such as the contents of your post, are shown. So taken in the larger context of literature, the machine is alien to us metaphor breaks down when we begin comparing it to other sources that are explicitly challenging the boundaries between our own nature and the nature of machines. Consider for example, the Matrix Trilogy, A.D. Police Files, Bubblegum Crisis, any of the various iterations of Ghost in the Shell (although Stand Alone Complex is probably the most pertinent), Ergo Proxy, Psycho Pass, and, of course, what you've already posted, among other titles. (And of course some of these titles actually appear as &quot;inspirational material&quot; so I'm thinking that the usage machine imagery is primarily thematic rather than metaphorical.)<br /> <br /> Now it may be the case that you believe the authors intention was something other than using machines as a metaphor for alienness (and it might be the case that the authors believe this themselves). That falls into the &quot;all bets are off&quot; YMMV category of argumentation.<br /> <br /> On the whole folks seem to have a penchant for seeing metaphors (and analogies) everywhere but that isn't always the work that any particular bit of imagery is doing at any particular point in a text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T10:21:18-07:00","id":873162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=873068#post873068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Show true wisdom and walk away.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It hasn't gone where I thought it would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T14:50:38-07:00","id":873307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=873070#post873070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Check your high school chemistry book again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Had to return it at the end of the school year a decade ago, so no luck.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The metaphor breaks down at multiple points. When you're positive that you can't find any of them, then check back with me again. </div> </div> </div>See above and share with the rest of the class if the imperfection of metaphors when applied comprehensively is not the whole of your point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T15:48:45-07:00","id":873347,"title":"","content":"It must be noted that God-Machine/Demon Developer Rose Bailey has gone on record saying that her primary source of inspiration for the God-machine was this sense of how people's entire lives, through the fault of no one, seemed to placed into certain ruts and forms, that a person's life was dictated from birth to death by the accidents of systems upon systems laid before, during, and after, that their successes, failures, swings of good fortune and ladder climbling, their falls of luck and casting from the echelons of the society-these things happen, not at the fault of any given person, but merely the order of reality. The pervasive sense, that these things that happened without purpose or malice, served <i>something</i>, some <i>end</i>, is a big point of birth for the God-Machine, and is in fact why the God-machine is actually <i>not</i> a machine, so much as an impossibly colossal sense of <i>order</i>, the presence of a <i>plan</i>, and the accompanying implication of a <i>will,</i> all balanced by the simple horror of a clock.<br /> <br /> This is one of quite a lot of metaphors that make up the soul and skin of Demon the Descent and it's monsters, who walk the crossroads of flesh, machine, and spirit between the heavens of the divine and the earths of &quot;merely beyond humanity&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T15:59:10-07:00","id":873356,"title":"","content":"Which is a sense I love, and endeavor to keep, while removing bits of tech-gnostic that annoy my partner and my other players. Also, some simple... elemental and celestial-based Exploits, and some name changes, have helped alleviate that, while keeping what I see as the soul of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T16:10:32-07:00","id":873365,"title":"","content":"I understand that?<br /> <br /> But like I said, it's not just part of the skin of the game, it's also part of the soul-or, perhaps, the question of soullessness.<br /> <br /> I've talked before, in the Changeling Demon thread of yore, about how that techgnostic 'skin' goes deep down, and I still feel like I haven't even properly scratched the surface of that subject.<br /> <br /> Descent can run without the machine part, in fairness. Fully capable of it. But it's richer, more dynamic, more poignant(and more fun!) if you dig beyond &quot;Oh, it's like the Matrix&quot; and go into the actual techgnosis and the several points of it. <br /> <br /> But then again, I actually <i>did</i> read Erik Davis's Techgnosis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T16:23:01-07:00","id":873371,"title":"","content":"While I read Techgnosis, also. (good book) I just enjoy mysticism as much. It's not inherently bad to (and I keep the God-Machine in my world, remember. I just add Fallen characteristics to angels, demons, and the mythology.) but I understand being unsatisfied with it.<br /> <br /> Though, I'm interested in what you mean when you say it goes deep? I'm interested in hearing more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T16:23:21-07:00","id":873372,"title":"","content":"Some people the tech part of techgnostic will speak to and enrich the gnostic themes, others it will not speak to and only distract from them. Personally I encourage anyone who hasn't to give the techgnostisism a try, because I firmly believe if you go deeper than the asthetic and look at what the game is trying to say with its use of machines, it greatly improves the game overall. But I also firmly believe that if you thoroughly dislike that Matrix-y asthetic and feel it's going to distract from the gnostic themes, you're better off doing away with them and playing up the spiritual parts of Descent than throwing the baby out with the bath water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T16:26:16-07:00","id":873373,"title":"","content":"That's a fair way to put it. I ran a Descent game for my group, and then played in one. My player's still say it distracts from it, hence, my hack. In short, I agree with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T17:20:39-07:00","id":873398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=873372#post873372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some people the tech part of techgnostic will speak to and enrich the gnostic themes, others it will not speak to and only distract from them. Personally I encourage anyone who hasn't to give the techgnostisism a try, because I firmly believe if you go deeper than the asthetic and look at what the game is trying to say with its use of machines, it greatly improves the game overall. But I also firmly believe that if you thoroughly dislike that Matrix-y asthetic and feel it's going to distract from the gnostic themes, you're better off doing away with them and playing up the spiritual parts of Descent than throwing the baby out with the bath water.</div> </div> </div> </div>How exactly does one &quot;give techgnosticism a try?&quot; Read Techgnosis? I'm legitimately curious, because I feel like my lack of exposure to a lot of literature hurts my understanding of these games sometimes and I'm left with superficial understandings of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T19:27:41-07:00","id":873468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=873398#post873398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How exactly does one &quot;give techgnosticism a try?&quot; Read Techgnosis? I'm legitimately curious, because I feel like my lack of exposure to a lot of literature hurts my understanding of these games sometimes and I'm left with superficial understandings of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's an option, joining a game that's run with the tech aspects incorporated is a good way to see it run firsthand. Actual Plays can be a good alternative if you can't find a game to join. If you're looking to learn more about Gnosticism and how technology is a good analogy for it, there are lots of philosophy books on the subject. <i>Techgnosis</i> is one, but even something like <i>The Matrix and Philosophy</i>. Gnosticism is a big theme in a lot of cyberpunk, so pick your favorite piece of cyberpunk media and consume it with a mind towards how it could be viewed through the lense of Gnosticism. Read up on Gnosticism with a mind towards how it could be viewed through a technological lens.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest, cyberpunk and Gnosticism are such an intuitive match for me that it's difficult to recommend ways to delve deeper into the connections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T21:51:52-07:00","id":873530,"title":"","content":"Neuromancer, the defining cyberpunk novel, should be read by everyone thinking of doing God-Machine games and twice by anyone thinking of doing Demon games.<br /> <br /> And yes, you will find more than a healthy heaping of techgnosticism in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T07:42:06-07:00","id":875623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=873307#post873307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had to return it at the end of the school year a decade ago, so no luck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so basically the dog ate my homework...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=873307#post873307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See above and share with the rest of the class if the imperfection of metaphors when applied comprehensively is not the whole of your point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll get back to you either late this week or early next (slammed with conference deadlines and annual reviews and this &quot;unpacking&quot; requires a tl;dr). In the mean time I'd rethink the metaphor. Consider, for instance just how many possible energy levels an electron could occupy. Consider also whether or not demons are still angels and how electrons remain electrons even after they lose some energy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T14:41:07-07:00","id":876003,"title":"","content":"Technognosticism is hard because the idea is that the God-Machine knows the Truth about how physics, maths, whatever works for real (by &quot;for real&quot; I mean without any supernatural trick whilst having a complete understanding of how the universe works). Imagine this: if you could go back to the middle ages with your laptop computer and show it around, there is no way you could explain to them it's not magical. And it's not. So, how we're going to translate into a story a technology that stems from the True and Definitive laws of the Fallen World that, if we had to face it, we would be as clueless and as awed than a medieval guy would be before a laptop ? The answer in D:tD is the Occult Matrix: a chain of events leading to an effect using &quot;actual&quot; physics laws mankind don't understand yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","user":"JPS","date":". 04-27-2016, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T20:29:29-07:00","id":876222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JPS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=876003#post876003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technognosticism is hard because the idea is that the God-Machine knows the Truth about how physics, maths, whatever works for real (by &amp;quot;for real&amp;quot; I mean without any supernatural trick whilst having a complete understanding of how the universe works). Imagine this: if you could go back to the middle ages with your laptop computer and show it around, there is no way you could explain to them it's not magical. And it's not. So, how we're going to translate into a story a technology that stems from the True and Definitive laws of the Fallen World that, if we had to face it, we would be as clueless and as awed than a medieval guy would be before a laptop ? The answer in D:tD is the Occult Matrix: a chain of events leading to an effect using &amp;quot;actual&amp;quot; physics laws mankind don't understand yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clarke's third law is a fundamental aspect of techgnostisism. Both in the that it is one of the the foundations on which the ideas are based, and in the sense that it's one of the most basic truths of the philosophy, beyond which one can delve much deeper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T20:42:33-07:00","id":879873,"title":"","content":"So I've been considering starting a thread that does some retelling of bible stories (and maybe some other fire and brimstone tales) using DtD, for the purpose of showing how DtD can be religious without removing anything or going to Demon the Fallen. That said I've yet to have tuits to actually write anything on that, but if people wanted to start the thread and contribute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T20:51:33-07:00","id":879876,"title":"","content":"I'd be interested! I'd love to see what can be done, and how it'd look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT