&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T20:40:09-07:00","id":880709,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/880707-god-and-demons-of-biblical-proportions\">Started Thread</a>. My work is liable to be horrendous so hopefully others contribute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T07:19:56-07:00","id":880955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JPS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=876003#post876003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technognosticism is hard because the idea is that the God-Machine knows the Truth about how physics, maths, whatever works for real (by &quot;for real&quot; I mean without any supernatural trick whilst having a complete understanding of how the universe works). Imagine this: if you could go back to the middle ages with your laptop computer and show it around, there is no way you could explain to them it's not magical. And it's not. So, how we're going to translate into a story a technology that stems from the True and Definitive laws of the Fallen World that, if we had to face it, we would be as clueless and as awed than a medieval guy would be before a laptop ? The answer in D:tD is the Occult Matrix: a chain of events leading to an effect using &quot;actual&quot; physics laws mankind don't understand yet.</div> </div> </div> </div> A bit late, but my 2 cents on this issue. <br /> <br /> The God Machine isn't doing anything new or &quot;real&quot; to the laws of physics/math. What the God Machine is doing is taking the flow and manuipulation of Essence into account when doing its science. We all know that spirits can do virtually anything with their essence, depending on their nature. The God Machine is using Essence to do all the things that other ephemeral beings can naturally do, but does so in a way ghosts, spirits, etc do not. So, when the God Machine uses its Infrastructure to alter the world's fate, its doing so by calculating the impact of all the different influences of Essence (Sol/Luna, local mages stemming geomantic flows, werewolves building loci, etc) and determining what needs to be done to make the Essence perform the necessary result. <br /> <br /> And that's how techgnosis works here. Machines that impact and manipulate the spiritual. Essence is literally the basis for everything spiritual in the CofD. And that's why Demons learn Embed through mediation and prayer - they're aligning their bio-mechanical &quot;souls&quot; with the flow of spiritual esssence and its resonance. <br /> <br /> This thread, back a year ago, talked about Clark's Third Law quite a bit, but I think that it missed something rather important. Yes, sufficently advanced technology is indistinguishable from magic <i>if you define magic as the unexplained</i>. So, yeah, in the past of the real world, people would call a laptop or tablet magical. However, the CofD doesn't define magic that way. In the Chronicles / World of Darkness, magic is synomous with the word &quot;occult&quot; in all its definitions. Magic is the &quot;hidden.&quot; Hidden knowledge, hidden spiecies, hidden phenomeon that are beyond the normal range of experience or observation abilities. While you can scientifically observe magic, in the CofD magic tries to hide itself (or has patrons that do the hiding) from humanity at large so that it can't be observed. So, while people in the past might call a tablet magic, they're misusing the word magic in this case. <br /> <br /> When you talk about techgnosis in terms of the CofD, we have to take that into account. Techgnosis is technology that deals with the hidden spiritual aspects of the world. Techgnosis is understanding that even modern technology has animistic spirits in it, that it has supernal resonance. Techgnosis is understanding that the old alchemy principles of spiritual purification holds still weight with modern advances. Its the understanding that technology in the CofD is literally magical, that your laptop, be it in the present day, in the distant past, in the far future, is magical and spiritual all at the same time. You just can't see the parts that are magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T08:45:06-07:00","id":884652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=873307#post873307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See above and share with the rest of the class if the imperfection of metaphors when applied comprehensively is not the whole of your point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the patience. Having finally dug myself out from under the end of semester/conference submission perfect storm of deadlines I'll &quot;unpack&quot; why the electron metaphor doesn't work. Apologies to all for the tl;dr and partially OT content of this post. For many of these quibbles I think we really should resort to PMs.<br /> <br /> A simple examination of the Angel falls and becomes Demon relationship shows that it's a binary one. And while an electron's energy gain or loss can cause it to transition from one energy level to another (up or down), it isn't as neat because higher mass atoms have much more complex sets of energy states (n Shells). The primary problem is that the system isn't binary. So if, in the metaphor the Demon's corporeal existence represents the 1 Shell then in the metaphor an Angel's ephemeral existence should be analogous the 2 Shell. The metaphor starts falling apart once we reach an element like Sodium which has 3 Shells, Potassium which has four, Rubidium (5), Cesium (6), etc. The implication here, if the metaphor works this way, is that there are states that are more ephemeral than the ephemeral state. <br /> <br /> Of course, you could argue that the metaphor is in fact referring to an electron's base state and excited state, but this has the same problem because electrons can have multiple levels of excited state (before the atom eventually loses them). The implication that there are states more ephemeral than the ephemeral state is still there.<br /> <br /> Now the metaphysicist in me just eats this stuff up. Suddenly we would have a massive super-metasetting (where super-metasetting is understood to be the whole continuum of CofD metasettings) scale mystery. But this leads us directly to problem number two with this metaphor. <br /> <br /> If there is a &quot;more ephemeral state&quot;, what narrative purpose is it supposed to serve? Are Angels themselves fallen from some other kind of entity? Does the narrative need this kind of obfuscating murk? <br /> <br /> From an editorial perspective, the answer is a pretty clean no. We don't need a &quot;more ephemeral state&quot;. But we already have a perfectly good ephemeral state to explore. A &quot;more ephemeral state&quot; doesn't add anything that we aren't already getting from some other portion of the game's prose and systems. Adding a &quot;more ephemeral state&quot; is simply bloat. It's adipose tissue that the game doesn't actually need. So as interesting as the metaphysical questions raised are, they're also completely unnecessary.<br /> <br /> Finally, the metaphor falls apart when one considers natural kinds. The game's prose takes very great pains to showcase how fundamentally different Demons (corporeal entities) and Angels (ephemeral entities) are from one another (they use completely different mechanical systems). Electrons, regardless of how much energy they gain or lose as they transition across energy levels, never stop being electrons. It's not the case that an electron blasts off a photon and suddenly becomes a proton (or vice versa). So the metaphor doesn't work here either.<br /> <br /> The real problem is that you're just not very good at using metaphors. The example you've chosen doesn't work on many levels. It's also actually so complex that it's really a half-baked analogy.<br /> <br /> We may have to consider that what happens when an Angel falls is too complex for any metaphor (Tier 1) to actually get the job done. What may be required is a detailed analogy (Tier 2). A good alternative is to liken an Angel to a high tension cable that runs between two points. In this case one end is the CofD world and the other is some CofD other-dimension. When the cable snaps (i.e., when an Angel falls) one part of it strikes the CofD world and a Demon is formed. Looked at in this way we can see that Demons are actually scars on the face of the CofD world. The implication is that there is some-other dimensional world where the other part of cable recoils to. This is very interesting because it implies that something happens to the rest of the Angelic stuff that doesn't become part of the Demon. We can say that it all goes back to the God-Machine and the God-Machine itself is this other dimensional space, it is Heaven so-to-speak. Getting lashed with the other end of that broken high-tension cable must leave scars on the face of Heaven too. What does that look like? Isn't discovering that a fantastic mystery to form a chronicle around? Could there be something, call them Seraphs, like the Deathlords and Spirit Gods that can't leave the God-Machine (much like Deathlords can't normally leave the Underworld and Spirit Gods can't leave the Shadow)? What does it mean if the God-Machine is a reality/setting onto itself just like the Underworld, the Shadow, the Supernal Realms, the Primordial Dream, etc.?<br /> <br /> Regarding the OP. I see the conversation has shaped up rather well. One can easily, if one wishes, eliminate the machine (and even the God) aspects from D:tD. The price may or may not be the loss of technogisticism. Recall that tying a rock to a stick with some vines is no less of a technological achievement than cutting an integrated circuit into a semi-conductor wafer with a laser.<br /> <br /> More food for thought, what does it mean that other simians, birds, otters, beavers, and even rodents also use tools? If wolf-packs unconsciously employ very sophisticated mathematical algorithms as they hunt, are Angels really any different from these natural (i.e., non-mechanical/artificial) things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T23:24:35-07:00","id":885202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=884652#post884652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A simple examination of the Angel falls and becomes Demon relationship shows that it's a binary one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look in the &quot;e&quot; section of the game's lexicon between &quot;Embed&quot; and &quot;Exploit&quot; and try again, please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T00:21:57-07:00","id":885229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=884652#post884652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real problem is that you're just not very good at using metaphors. The example you've chosen doesn't work on many levels. It's also actually so complex that it's really a half-baked analogy.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/YwgbT16.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T14:10:19-07:00","id":885684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=885202#post885202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look in the &amp;quot;e&amp;quot; section of the game's lexicon between &amp;quot;Embed&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Exploit&amp;quot; and try again, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>Naw. I'm not seeing it. If you really think this metaphor works then you need to spell it out. Examples?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T18:33:31-07:00","id":885859,"title":"","content":"I think we need to stop using metaphors with Jacob because he doesn't seem to ever grasp them.<br /> <br /> Also, the thing between angel and demon which they are referring to are exiles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 05-08-2016, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:13:53-07:00","id":886470,"title":"","content":"Just do what I do.<br /> <br /> \u200bDon't use Demon: The Descent and openly declare that the God-Machine doesn't exist in your games. If you're the ST, you have final say on such things. I don't like the God-Machine or Demon either (I don't like Fallen either, but that's another story) but I am thankful that New World of Darkness is a toolbox with no set canon or metaplot, so you can keep what you want and remove what you don't more easily.<br /> <br /> Hell, I still use 1e nWoD for my games if it helps, since the God-Machine didn't become a big thing until 2e. But if you like 2e mechanics, then don't play Demon: The Descent and play another 2e/CofD game. Simple as that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T13:08:01-07:00","id":886591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=886470#post886470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just do what I do.<br /> <br /> \u200bDon't use Demon: The Descent and openly declare that the God-Machine doesn't exist in your games. If you're the ST, you have final say on such things. I don't like the God-Machine or Demon either (I don't like Fallen either, but that's another story) but I am thankful that New World of Darkness is a toolbox with no set canon or metaplot, so you can keep what you want and remove what you don't more easily.<br /> <br /> Hell, I still use 1e nWoD for my games if it helps, since the God-Machine didn't become a big thing until 2e. But if you like 2e mechanics, then don't play Demon: The Descent and play another 2e/CofD game. Simple as that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The God-Machine is only a big deal in 2e if you're playing Demon or using the God-Machone Chronicle. If you're still using Vampire/Werewolf/Mage 1e because you're afraid of the God-Machine, it isn't there and you're missing out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T13:23:44-07:00","id":886602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=886591#post886591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The God-Machine is only a big deal in 2e if you're playing Demon or using the God-Machone Chronicle. If you're still using Vampire/Werewolf/Mage 1e because you're afraid of the God-Machine, it isn't there and you're missing out.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a long standing thing with Camilla. Just move on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T14:31:33-07:00","id":886638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=886591#post886591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The God-Machine is only a big deal in 2e if you're playing Demon or using the God-Machone Chronicle. If you're still using Vampire/Werewolf/Mage 1e because you're afraid of the God-Machine, it isn't there and you're missing out.</div> </div> </div> </div> I know the God-Machine doesn't affect Vampire 2e that much, but I just prefer the 1e mechanics. It's just a personal preference, nothing more, nothing less. I thought the 1e mechanics were sufficient enough. Again, all a matter of personal taste.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T14:50:08-07:00","id":886646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=886638#post886638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know the God-Machine doesn't affect Vampire 2e <b>at all</b>, but I just prefer the 1e mechanics. It's just a personal preference, nothing more, nothing less. I thought the 1e mechanics were sufficient enough. Again, all a matter of personal taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. If the requiem ST doesn't involves it, there isn't anything setting-wise that forces his hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T14:55:27-07:00","id":886651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=886646#post886646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Emphasis mine. If the requiem ST doesn't involves it, there isn't anything setting-wise that forces his hand.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bFair point, it's been a while since I've read 2e Requiem, you are right, there is no reference to the God-Machine and I agree with you on the ST having final say over the setting. There is nothing wrong with 2e, I just am more familiar and comfortable with 1e. Sorry if I upset anyone here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T14:58:59-07:00","id":886654,"title":"","content":"Nobody's upset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T14:59:38-07:00","id":886656,"title":"","content":"Oh, okay. Well, let's get back on topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T13:14:52-07:00","id":888495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=885859#post885859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we need to stop using metaphors with Jacob because he doesn't seem to ever grasp them.<br /> <br /> Also, the thing between angel and demon which they are referring to are exiles.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't be so sure that I don't know exactly what metaphors are if I were you. Looks can be quite deceptive. I'm not saying Angels and Demons are literally electrons after all. I'm just countering the metaphor by working within its confines. From where I'm sitting I'm not the one whose reading comprehension needs help. (Fact: there are entire branches of academia that eschew the use of metaphors because they frequently obfuscate as much as they clarify.) Clear, concise explication is always best. If you're to stop using metaphors (you in the plural sense for this sentence, not necessarily you specifically), I'd have it be because you realize that they're harder to use and not as helpful as you seem to think they are. But then again, if the only tool you have is a claw hammer then every problem looks like a nail.<br /> <br /> Not seeing how Exiles have a role in supporting the electron metaphor though. If anything their presence further damages its explicative power. Happy to be persuaded otherwise but you know, provide details. If tl;dr then don't be afraid to PM me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T14:02:23-07:00","id":888538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=888495#post888495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not seeing how Exiles have a role in supporting the electron metaphor though. If anything their presence further damages its explicative power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's a hint: binary states and the matter of whether or not a given portion of a whole continuum of beings that dwell in the material realm <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=80839#post80839\">at varying removes from &quot;God&quot;</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=815001#post815001\">can completely circumvent the manifestation rules</a> are ephemeral have nothing to with a metaphor that I used when <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=872776#post872776\">I was explicitly short on time</a> that you have somehow determined to be worth generating an extended argument about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>